/-! # Cohomology of a colimit of sites with finite coverings: systems of abelian sheaves and sections (Stacks 0EXZ, 09YN)

`CategoryTheory.Sites.InverseSystem.InverseSystemOfSites` requires every covering sieve of every
level to be **generated** by a finite family. That requirement is satisfied by no inverse system of
etale sites: over `Spec Q` the sieve generated by the family of all `Spec Q(sqrt d)`, `d`
squarefree, is a covering sieve, because one of its members is already a one-element etale covering
and a Grothendieck topology is upward closed, yet it is generated by no finite subfamily, since
each member of a finite generating family would factor through some `Spec Q(sqrt d_k)` and a
`Q`-algebra embedding between quadratic fields is an isomorphism. So a theorem whose hypothesis is
such a system cannot be instantiated for etale sites at all.

`InverseSystemOfFiniteSites` carries the source-faithful requirement instead (Stacks 00VH): every
covering sieve **contains** a finite covering family. The four files
`CohomologyOfColimitOfFiniteSites.AbelianSystemsAndSections`,
`CohomologyOfColimitOfFiniteSites.MorphismOfSitesAndDescent`,
`CohomologyOfColimitOfFiniteSites.CohomologyDiagram` and
`CohomologyOfColimitOfFiniteSites.CohomologyColimit` re-derive, for that structure, the chain of
results that Stacks 09YP depends on, so that Stacks 09YP becomes available for the systems
Stacks 0EYL produces. This first file contains the finiteness lemmas on the weak structure, the
systems of abelian sheaves on an inverse system of sites (Stacks 0EXZ) and the sections of a
colimit of sheaves on a colimit of sites (Stacks 09YN).

## Main results

* `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.AbelianSheafSystem.exists_mono_to_pointwise_injective`:
  **Stacks 0EXZ** for an inverse system of sites with finite coverings.
* `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.sections_colimit_pullback_of_colimit`:
  **Stacks 09YN** for such a system.

The further results of the chain are `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.exists_isMorphismOfSites_sections_pullback_of_colimit`
(**Stacks 0A35**) and the `pullbackPushforwardDesc` family (**Stacks 0EXJ**), in
`CohomologyOfColimitOfFiniteSites.MorphismOfSitesAndDescent`, and
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSiteCohomology.cohomologyCocone` with
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSiteCohomology.isColimitCohomologyCocone` (**Stacks 09YP**), in
`CohomologyOfColimitOfFiniteSites.CohomologyColimit`.

## Implementation notes

The strong field `InverseSystemOfSites.finiteCoverings` is consumed in exactly four places in the
strong development, and all four are discharged here from the weak field together with Stacks
00VH (3), the existence of the fibre products of a covering:

* at the descent of a covering of the colimit to a level, it is applied to the pullback of an
  already finitely generated sieve, and `StacksWeakAux.exists_finite_generating_pullback` supplies
  a finite generating family for such a pullback outright, with no finiteness hypothesis on the
  topology;
* at cover-preservation of `u_i`, a finite covering family contained in the covering sieve
  suffices, because the pushforward of the sieve it generates is a covering of the colimit and the
  pushforward is monotone;
* at continuity of `u_i`, `StacksWeakAux.toGrothendieck_inf_finite_eq` turns the weak field into
  the statement that the finite coverings *generate* `D.J i` as a Grothendieck topology, after
  which `CategoryTheory.Precoverage.isSheaf_toGrothendieck_iff` reduces the sheaf condition to the
  finite coverings and their pullbacks, which are finite by the first point;
* at the restriction of the system to the levels below `i`, the field is only reindexed.

Everything else is the strong development read at the weak structure: no statement is weakened,
and no hypothesis is added. The names of this file are disjoint from those of the strong
development, the site namespaces being `Stacks.WeakSites.*` rather than `Stacks.Sites.*`.

## References

* [Stacks 09YP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09YP)
* [Stacks 00VH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VH)
* [Stacks 0A34](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A34)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe uu1 uu2 uu3 ww

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Sites.InverseSystem Opposite

/-- The transition functor `u a` of an inverse system of sites with finite coverings is
continuous: continuity is one half of the `isMorphismOfSites` field. -/
theorem InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.continuous (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{uu1, uu2, uu3})
    {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) : (D.u a).IsContinuous (D.J j) (D.J i) :=
  (D.isMorphismOfSites a).isContinuous

namespace StacksWeakAux

/-- **The pullback of a finitely generated sieve is finitely generated**, as soon as the pullbacks
of the generators exist. No finiteness hypothesis on the topology enters: the pullback of
`Sieve.generate (Presieve.ofArrows W h)` along `ξ` is generated by the `ξ`-pullbacks of the `h a`,
which are indexed by the same finite type. -/
theorem exists_finite_generating_pullback {V : Type ww} [SmallCategory V]
    {Z T : V} {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (W : ι → V) (h : ∀ a, W a ⟶ Z) (ξ : T ⟶ Z)
    [(Presieve.ofArrows W h).HasPullbacks ξ] :
    ∃ (α : Type) (_ : Finite α) (B : α → V) (g : ∀ a, B a ⟶ T),
      Sieve.generate (Presieve.ofArrows B g) =
        (Sieve.generate (Presieve.ofArrows W h)).pullback ξ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, ⟨eqv⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin ι
  have hpb : ∀ a, Limits.HasPullback (h a) ξ := fun a =>
    Presieve.HasPullbacks.hasPullback ξ (Presieve.ofArrows.mk a)
  refine ⟨Fin n, inferInstance, fun k => Limits.pullback (h (eqv.symm k)) ξ,
    fun k => Limits.pullback.snd (h (eqv.symm k)) ξ, le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
  · rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff]
    rintro A r ⟨k⟩
    exact ⟨W (eqv.symm k), Limits.pullback.fst (h (eqv.symm k)) ξ, h (eqv.symm k),
      Presieve.ofArrows.mk (eqv.symm k), Limits.pullback.condition⟩
  · rw [← Sieve.pullbackArrows_comm, Sieve.generate_le_iff]
    rintro A r ⟨B', hh, hmem⟩
    obtain ⟨a⟩ := hmem
    obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ : ∃ k, eqv.symm k = a := ⟨eqv a, by simp⟩
    exact Sieve.le_generate _ _ _ (Presieve.ofArrows.mk k)

/-- **A finite presieve is a finite family of arrows.** `Precoverage.finite` asks the uncurried
presieve to be a finite set, and that set indexes the family. -/
theorem exists_ofArrows_of_mem_finite {V : Type ww} [SmallCategory V] {Y₀ : V} (S : Presieve Y₀)
    (hfin : S ∈ Precoverage.finite V Y₀) :
    ∃ (α : Type ww) (_ : Finite α) (B : α → V) (g : ∀ p, B p ⟶ Y₀),
      S = Presieve.ofArrows B g := by
  have h : S.uncurry.Finite := hfin
  refine ⟨S.uncurry, h.to_subtype, fun p => p.1.1, fun p => p.1.2, le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
  · exact fun W f hf => Presieve.ofArrows.mk' (⟨⟨W, f⟩, hf⟩ : S.uncurry) rfl (by simp)
  · rintro W f ⟨p⟩
    exact p.2

/-- **The finite coverings of a system with finite coverings generate its topology.** This is the
field `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.finiteCoverings` — every covering sieve contains a finite
covering family — read as an equality of Grothendieck topologies, which is the form the sheaf
condition is reduced along. -/
theorem toGrothendieck_inf_finite_eq (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{uu1, uu2, uu3}) (i : D.I) :
    ((D.J i).toPrecoverage ⊓ Precoverage.finite (D.C i)).toGrothendieck = D.J i := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [Precoverage.toGrothendieck_eq_sInf]
    exact sInf_le fun X S hS => (GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff _ _).1 hS.1
  · intro X S hS
    obtain ⟨R, hRS, hRcov, hRfin⟩ := D.finiteCoverings i S hS
    exact ((D.J i).toPrecoverage ⊓ Precoverage.finite (D.C i)).toGrothendieck.superset_covering
      ((Sieve.generate_le_iff _ _).2 hRS)
      (Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck ⟨hRcov, hRfin⟩)

end StacksWeakAux

end

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe v u w t z

namespace InverseSystemOfFiniteSites

/-- Direct image of abelian sheaves along a transition morphism in an inverse system of sites. -/
noncomputable def abelianSheafPushforward (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) :
    Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t}) ⥤ Sheaf (D.J j) (Ab.{max u v w t}) :=
  letI := D.continuous a
  (D.u a).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Ab.{max u v w t}) (D.J j) (D.J i)

/-- Abelian sheaves on each site of an inverse system of sites admit sheafification at the
coefficient universe `max u v w t`. Not an instance: a conclusion whose universe is a `max`
with a free summand leaves instance search with a universe constraint it cannot solve, so the
fact is supplied where it is needed. -/
theorem hasSheafifyAb (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w}) (i : D.I) :
    HasSheafify (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t}) :=
  have : PreservesFilteredColimitsOfSize.{w, w} (forget (Ab.{max u v w t})) :=
    preservesFilteredColimitsOfSize_shrink _
  inferInstance

/-- Inverse image of abelian sheaves along a transition morphism. -/
noncomputable def abelianSheafPullback (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) :
    Sheaf (D.J j) (Ab.{max u v w t}) ⥤ Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t}) :=
  letI := D.continuous a
  haveI := hasSheafifyAb.{v, u, w, t} D i
  (D.u a).sheafPullback (Ab.{max u v w t}) (D.J j) (D.J i)

/-- Inverse image is adjoint to direct image for abelian sheaves. -/
noncomputable def abelianSheafAdjunction (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) :
    abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a ⊣ abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a :=
  letI := D.continuous a
  haveI := hasSheafifyAb.{v, u, w, t} D i
  (D.u a).sheafAdjunctionContinuous (Ab.{max u v w t}) (D.J j) (D.J i)

/-- The inverse image of abelian sheaves along a transition morphism preserves monomorphisms:
the transitions of an inverse system of sites are morphisms of sites, and exactness of the
inverse image is independent of the universe of the sections. -/
theorem abelianSheafPullback_preservesMonomorphisms (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) :
    (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).PreservesMonomorphisms := by
  let _ := D.continuous a
  have := hasSheafifyAb.{v, u, w, t} D i
  have h : ((D.u a).sheafPullback (Ab.{max u v w t}) (D.J j) (D.J i)).PreservesMonomorphisms :=
    Stacks.Sites.AbelianPullback.preservesMonomorphisms_sheafPullback_ab_largeSections.{max u v t,
      w} (D.isMorphismOfSites a)
  exact h

/-- Direct image along a transition morphism preserves injective abelian sheaves. This is
Stacks 0730 for abelian sheaves: the inverse image is exact, so its right adjoint preserves
injectives. -/
theorem injective_abelianSheafPushforward (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (A : Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) [Injective A] :
    Injective ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).obj A) :=
  have := abelianSheafPullback_preservesMonomorphisms.{v, u, w, t} D a
  have := Functor.preservesInjectiveObjects_of_adjunction_of_preservesMonomorphisms
    (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D a)
  Functor.injective_obj _ _

/-- Abelian sheaves on each site of an inverse system of sites have enough injectives. -/
theorem enoughInjectives (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w}) (i : D.I) :
    EnoughInjectives (Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) :=
  have := hasSheafifyAb.{v, u, w, t} D i
  have : EssentiallySmall.{max u v w t} (D.C i) := inferInstance
  CategoryTheory.Sheaf.enoughInjectives_addCommGrpCat (D.J i)

/-- The canonical comparison between successive direct images and direct image along the
composite transition. -/
noncomputable def abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j k : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k) :
    abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a ⋙ abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b ≅
      abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) := by
  dsimp [abelianSheafPushforward]
  letI := D.continuous a
  letI := D.continuous b
  letI := D.continuous (a ≫ b)
  exact Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousComp'
    (eqToIso (D.comp a b).symm) (Ab.{max u v w t}) (D.J k) (D.J j) (D.J i)

/-- The canonical comparison between inverse image along a composite transition and successive
inverse images, obtained from the direct-image comparison by uniqueness of left adjoints. -/
noncomputable def abelianSheafPullbackCompIso (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j k : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k) :
    abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b ⋙ abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a ≅
      abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) :=
  (((abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D b).comp
    (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D a)).ofNatIsoRight
      (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b)).leftAdjointUniq
    (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b))

/-- The canonical identification of the identity functor with direct image along an identity
transition. -/
noncomputable def abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (i : D.I) :
    Functor.id (Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) ≅
      abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i) := by
  dsimp [abelianSheafPushforward]
  letI := D.continuous (𝟙 i)
  exact (Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousId (Ab.{max u v w t}) (D.J i)).symm ≪≫
    (Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousIso
      (eqToIso (D.id_map i)) (Ab.{max u v w t}) (D.J i) (D.J i)).symm

/-- The canonical comparison of inverse image along an identity with the identity functor. -/
noncomputable def abelianSheafPullbackIdIso (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (i : D.I) : abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i) ≅ 𝟭 (Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) :=
  (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).leftAdjointUniq
    (Adjunction.id.ofNatIsoRight (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i))

section CompIsoSections

private lemma pushforwardCompIso_inv_app_app (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j k : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k)
    (X : Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (U : D.C k) :
    (((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).inv.app X).hom.app (Opposite.op U)) =
      X.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg Opposite.op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp a b) U))) := by
  let _ := D.continuous a
  let _ := D.continuous b
  let _ := D.continuous (a ≫ b)
  dsimp [abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso, abelianSheafPushforward]
  exact sheafPushforwardContinuousComp'_inv_app_app.{w, max u v w t} (D.comp a b).symm
    (D.J k) (D.J j) (D.J i) X U

private lemma pushforwardCompIso_hom_app_app (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j k : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k)
    (X : Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (U : D.C k) :
    (((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).hom.app X).hom.app (Opposite.op U)) =
      X.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg Opposite.op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp a b).symm U))) := by
  let _ := D.continuous a
  let _ := D.continuous b
  let _ := D.continuous (a ≫ b)
  dsimp [abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso, abelianSheafPushforward]
  exact sheafPushforwardContinuousComp'_hom_app_app.{w, max u v w t} (D.comp a b).symm
    (D.J k) (D.J j) (D.J i) X U

private lemma pushforwardIdIso_inv_app_app (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (i : D.I) (X : Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (U : D.C i) :
    (((abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app X).hom.app (Opposite.op U)) =
      X.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg Opposite.op (Functor.congr_obj (D.id_map i) U))) := by
  dsimp [abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso, abelianSheafPushforward]
  simp only [Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousIso_hom, eqToIso.inv,
    Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousNatTrans_app_hom, ObjectProperty.ι_obj,
    Functor.whiskerRight_app, Functor.op_obj, Functor.id_obj, NatTrans.op_app, eqToHom_app,
    eqToHom_op, Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousId, Iso.refl_hom, NatTrans.id_app,
    ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.id_hom]
  exact Category.comp_id _

private lemma pushforwardIdIso_hom_app_app (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (i : D.I) (X : Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (U : D.C i) :
    (((abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app X).hom.app (Opposite.op U)) =
      X.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg Opposite.op (Functor.congr_obj (D.id_map i).symm U))) := by
  dsimp [abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso, abelianSheafPushforward]
  simp only [Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousId, Iso.refl_inv, NatTrans.id_app,
    ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.id_hom, Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousIso_inv, eqToIso.hom,
    Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousNatTrans_app_hom, ObjectProperty.ι_obj,
    Functor.whiskerRight_app, Functor.op_obj, Functor.id_obj, NatTrans.op_app, eqToHom_app,
    eqToHom_op]
  exact Category.id_comp _

end CompIsoSections

/-- A system of abelian sheaves on an inverse system of sites, with inverse-image
transition maps. -/
structure AbelianSheafSystem (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w}) where
  /-- The abelian sheaf at an index. -/
  obj : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})
  /-- The inverse-image transition morphism. -/
  map : ∀ {i j} (a : i ⟶ j), (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).obj (obj j) ⟶ obj i
  /-- The transition along an identity is the canonical identity map. -/
  map_id : ∀ i, (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app (obj i) ≫ map (𝟙 i) =
    𝟙 (obj i)
  /-- Compatibility of transition morphisms with composition. -/
  map_comp : ∀ {i j k} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k),
    (abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).inv.app (obj k) ≫
      (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map (map b) ≫ map a = map (a ≫ b)

/-- A morphism of systems of abelian sheaves. -/
structure AbelianSheafSystem.Hom {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w}}
    (F G : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) where
  /-- The morphism at each index. -/
  app : ∀ i, F.obj i ⟶ G.obj i
  /-- Compatibility with the transition morphisms. -/
  naturality : ∀ {i j} (a : i ⟶ j),
    (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map (app j) ≫ G.map a = F.map a ≫ app i

namespace AbelianSheafSystem

/-- The arrows of the index category with a fixed target, indexing the product in the
construction of Stacks 0EXZ. -/
private abbrev Incoming (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w}) (i : D.I) :=
  Σ k : D.I, k ⟶ i

/-- A chosen injective abelian sheaf containing the sheaf of the system at an index. -/
private noncomputable def injectiveEnvelope (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (F : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) (i : D.I) :
    Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t}) :=
  letI := enoughInjectives.{v, u, w, t} D i
  Injective.under (F.obj i)

/-- A factor `f_{b,*} A_k` of the product `G_i` of the source's proof. -/
private noncomputable def incomingFactor (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (i : D.I) (b : Incoming D i) :
    Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t}) :=
  (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1)

attribute [local implicit_reducible] incomingFactor injectiveEnvelope

/-- The product `G_i = ∏_{b : k ⟶ i} f_{b,*} A_k` of the source's proof. -/
private noncomputable abbrev productObject (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (i : D.I) :
    Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t}) := ∏ᶜ (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i)

/-- The canonical map `f_a⁻¹ f_{b ∘ a,*} A_k ⟶ f_{b,*} A_k` on a single factor. -/
private noncomputable def incomingRestriction (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j)
    (b : Incoming D i) :
    (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).obj
      ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (b.2 ≫ a)).obj (A b.1)) ⟶
    (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1) :=
  ((abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D a).homEquiv _ _).symm
    ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 a).inv.app (A b.1))

private lemma incomingRestriction_homEquiv (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j)
    (b : Incoming D i) :
    (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D a).homEquiv
      ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (b.2 ≫ a)).obj (A b.1))
      ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1))
      (incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A a b) =
    (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 a).inv.app (A b.1) :=
  Equiv.apply_symm_apply _ _

private lemma pullbackIdIso_inv_counit (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (i : D.I) (X : Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) :
    (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).obj X) ≫
      (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).counit.app X =
    (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app X := by
  let adjId := Adjunction.id.ofNatIsoRight
    (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i)
  let adj := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)
  rw [abelianSheafPullbackIdIso, Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq_inv_app]
  simp [CategoryTheory.Adjunction.ofNatIsoRight, CategoryTheory.Adjunction.id]

private lemma incomingRestriction_id (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (i : D.I) (b : Incoming D i) :
    (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (b.2 ≫ 𝟙 i)).obj (A b.1)) ≫
      incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (𝟙 i) b =
    (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 (𝟙 i)).inv.app (A b.1) ≫
      (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1)) := by
  let g := (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 (𝟙 i)).inv.app (A b.1)
  rw [incomingRestriction, Adjunction.homEquiv_counit]
  have hnat :
      (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (b.2 ≫ 𝟙 i)).obj (A b.1)) ≫
        (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).map
          ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 (𝟙 i)).inv.app (A b.1)) =
      (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 (𝟙 i)).inv.app (A b.1) ≫
        (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).obj
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1))) := by
    simpa using
      ((abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.naturality g).symm
  calc
    _ = ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 (𝟙 i)).inv.app (A b.1) ≫
        (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).obj
            ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1)))) ≫
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).counit.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1)) := by
      calc
        _ = (g ≫ (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
              ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).obj
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1)))) ≫
              (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).counit.app
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1)) :=
          congrArg (fun q => q ≫
            (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).counit.app
              ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1))) hnat
        _ = _ := by rfl
    _ = (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 (𝟙 i)).inv.app (A b.1) ≫
        (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1)) := by
      rw [Category.assoc, pullbackIdIso_inv_counit]

private lemma pushforwardEqToIso_hom_app_app (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j : D.I} {a b : i ⟶ j} (e : a = b)
    (X : Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (U : (D.C j)ᵒᵖ) :
    ((eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D) e)).hom.app X).hom.app U =
      eqToHom (congrArg
        (fun g => ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D g).obj X).obj.obj U) e) := by
  subst e
  simp

private lemma abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso_assoc (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j k l : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k) (c : k ⟶ l) :
    (Functor.isoWhiskerLeft (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a)
        (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b c) ≪≫
      abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a (b ≫ c)) =
    (Functor.associator _ _ _).symm ≪≫
      Functor.isoWhiskerRight (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b)
        (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D c) ≪≫
      abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) c ≪≫
        eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D)
          (Category.assoc a b c)) := by
  apply Iso.ext
  apply NatTrans.ext
  funext X
  apply Sheaf.hom_ext
  apply NatTrans.ext
  funext U
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Functor.isoWhiskerLeft_hom, Functor.isoWhiskerRight_hom,
    Iso.symm_hom, NatTrans.comp_app, Functor.whiskerLeft_app, Functor.whiskerRight_app,
    Functor.associator_inv_app]
  change
    ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b c).hom.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).obj X)).hom.app U ≫
        ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a (b ≫ c)).hom.app X).hom.app U =
      ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D c).map
            ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).hom.app X)).hom.app U ≫
        ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) c).hom.app X).hom.app U ≫
          ((eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D)
            (Category.assoc a b c))).hom.app X).hom.app U
  rw [pushforwardCompIso_hom_app_app.{v, u, w, t} D b c _ U.unop,
    pushforwardCompIso_hom_app_app.{v, u, w, t} D a (b ≫ c) X U.unop,
    pushforwardEqToIso_hom_app_app.{v, u, w, t} D (Category.assoc a b c) X U]
  dsimp [abelianSheafPushforward, Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuous]
  rw [pushforwardCompIso_hom_app_app.{v, u, w, t} D a b X ((D.u c).obj U.unop),
    pushforwardCompIso_hom_app_app.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) c X U.unop]
  simp only [eqToHom_unop, eqToHom_map, eqToHom_op, eqToHom_trans, Functor.comp_obj,
    eqToHom_trans_assoc]
  exact (eqToHom_trans _ _).symm

private lemma abelianSheafPullbackCompIso_eqToIso (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j k l : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k) (c : k ⟶ l)
    {q : i ⟶ l} (e : (a ≫ b) ≫ c = q) :
    Adjunction.leftAdjointCompIso
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D c)
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b))
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D q)
        (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) c ≪≫
          eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D) e)) =
      Adjunction.leftAdjointCompIso
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D c)
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b))
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D ((a ≫ b) ≫ c))
        (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) c) ≪≫
      eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D) e) := by
  cases e
  simp

private lemma abelianSheafPullbackCompIso_eq_leftAdjointCompIso
    (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w}) {i j k : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k) :
    abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b =
      Adjunction.leftAdjointCompIso
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D b)
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D a)
        (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b))
        (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b) := by
  ext X
  simp [abelianSheafPullbackCompIso, Adjunction.leftAdjointCompIso,
    Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq, Adjunction.ofNatIsoRight]

private lemma abelianSheafPullbackCompIso_assoc (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {i j k l : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k) (c : k ⟶ l) :
    (Functor.isoWhiskerLeft (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D c)
        (abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b) ≪≫
      abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) c) ≪≫
      eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D) (Category.assoc a b c)) =
    (Functor.associator _ _ _).symm ≪≫
      Functor.isoWhiskerRight (abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b c)
        (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a) ≪≫
      abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a (b ≫ c) := by
  let adjC := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D c
  let adjAB := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b)
  let adjLeft := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D ((a ≫ b) ≫ c)
  let adjRight := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ (b ≫ c))
  let cmp := abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b) c
  have hchange :
      Adjunction.leftAdjointCompIso adjC adjAB adjRight
          (cmp ≪≫ eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D)
            (Category.assoc a b c))) =
        Adjunction.leftAdjointCompIso adjC adjAB adjLeft cmp ≪≫
          eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D)
            (Category.assoc a b c)) := by
    simpa [adjC, adjAB, adjLeft, adjRight, cmp] using
      abelianSheafPullbackCompIso_eqToIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b c
        (q := a ≫ (b ≫ c)) (Category.assoc a b c)
  have h := Adjunction.leftAdjointCompIso_assoc adjC
    (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D b)
    (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D a)
    (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (b ≫ c)) adjAB adjRight
    (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b c)
    (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b)
    (cmp ≪≫ eqToIso (congrArg (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D)
      (Category.assoc a b c)))
    (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a (b ≫ c))
    (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso_assoc.{v, u, w, t} D a b c)
  rw [hchange] at h
  simpa only [abelianSheafPullbackCompIso_eq_leftAdjointCompIso,
    ← Iso.trans_assoc] using h

/-- The transition morphism `f_a⁻¹ G_i ⟶ G_j` of the product system. -/
private noncomputable def productTransition (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) :
    (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).obj
      (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A j) ⟶ productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i :=
  Limits.Pi.lift fun b =>
    (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
      (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A j) ⟨b.1, b.2 ≫ a⟩) ≫
        incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A a b

private lemma productTransition_π (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j)
    (b : Incoming D i) :
    productTransition.{v, u, w, t} D A a ≫
        Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b =
      (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
        (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A j) ⟨b.1, b.2 ≫ a⟩) ≫
          incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A a b :=
  Limits.Pi.lift_comp_π _ _

private lemma siteFunctor_comp_id (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {k i : D.I} (b : k ⟶ i) :
    D.comp b (𝟙 i) =
      (congrArg (fun f : k ⟶ i => D.u f) (Category.comp_id b)).trans
        (by rw [D.id_map i, Functor.id_comp]) :=
  Subsingleton.elim _ _

private lemma pushforwardCompId_inv_cancels (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    {k i : D.I} (b : k ⟶ i) (X : Sheaf (D.J k) (Ab.{max u v w t})) :
    (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b (𝟙 i)).inv.app X ≫
      (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).obj X) =
      eqToHom (congrArg (fun F => F.obj X)
        (show abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (b ≫ 𝟙 i) =
            abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b by
          rw [Category.comp_id])) := by
  apply Sheaf.hom_ext
  apply NatTrans.ext
  funext U
  show ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b (𝟙 i)).inv.app X).hom.app U ≫
      ((abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).obj X)).hom.app U = _
  rw [pushforwardCompIso_inv_app_app.{v, u, w, t} D b (𝟙 i) X U.unop,
    pushforwardIdIso_inv_app_app.{v, u, w, t} D i
      ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).obj X) U.unop]
  rw [sheafEqToHom_hom_app]
  simp [abelianSheafPushforward, Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuous, eqToHom_map,
    eqToHom_trans]

private lemma incomingRestriction_comp (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t}))
    {i j k : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k) (c : Incoming D i) :
    (abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).inv.app
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D ((c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b)).obj (A c.1)) ≫
      (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
        (incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A b
            (show Incoming D j from ⟨c.1, c.2 ≫ a⟩)) ≫
      incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A a c =
    (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b)).map
        (eqToHom (congrArg
          (fun f => (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D f).obj (A c.1))
          (Category.assoc c.2 a b))) ≫
      incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (a ≫ b) c := by
  let adjA := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D a
  let adjB := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D b
  let adjAB := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b)
  let push := abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b
  let adjComp := (adjB.comp adjA).ofNatIsoRight push
  let c₁ : Incoming D j := ⟨c.1, c.2 ≫ a⟩
  let rB := incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A b c₁
  let rA := incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A a c
  have hUnitA := adjA.unit.naturality rB
  have hIso : abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b =
      Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq adjComp adjAB := by
    ext X
    simp [abelianSheafPullbackCompIso, adjA, adjB, adjAB, push, adjComp,
      Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq,
      Adjunction.ofNatIsoRight]
  apply (adjAB.homEquiv _ _).injective
  calc
    adjAB.homEquiv _ _
        ((abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).inv.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D ((c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b)).obj (A c.1)) ≫
          (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
            (incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A b
              (show Incoming D j from ⟨c.1, c.2 ≫ a⟩)) ≫
          incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A a c) = _ := by
      rw [hIso, Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq_inv_app,
        Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_right,
        Adjunction.homEquiv_leftAdjointUniq_hom_app]
      rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_left, incomingRestriction_homEquiv]
      simp only [Functor.comp_obj, Adjunction.ofNatIsoRight, NatTrans.comp_app, Functor.id_obj,
        Adjunction.comp_unit_app, Functor.whiskerLeft_app, Category.assoc, Lean.Elab.WF.paramLet,
        Functor.map_comp, adjComp, adjB, adjA]
      rw [← Functor.map_comp,
        ← push.hom.naturality
          ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rB ≫ rA)]
      simp only [Functor.comp_map]
      have hUnitA' :
          adjA.unit.app ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b).obj
              ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D ((c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b)).obj (A c.1))) ≫
            (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
              ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rB) =
          rB ≫ adjA.unit.app
            ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (c.2 ≫ a)).obj (A c.1)) := by
        simp [rB, c₁]
      have hExpand₁ :
          (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
              ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
                ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rB ≫ rA)) =
            (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
                  ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rB)) ≫
              (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rA) := by
        rw [Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp]
      have hCombine₁ :
          (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map (adjA.unit.app
              ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b).obj
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D ((c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b)).obj (A c.1)))) ≫
            (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
              ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
                ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rB)) =
          (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
            (adjA.unit.app ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b).obj
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D ((c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b)).obj (A c.1))) ≫
              (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
                ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rB)) := by
        rw [← Functor.map_comp]
      have hExpand₂ :
          (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
              (rB ≫ adjA.unit.app
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (c.2 ≫ a)).obj (A c.1))) =
            (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map rB ≫
              (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
                (adjA.unit.app
                  ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (c.2 ≫ a)).obj (A c.1))) := by
        rw [Functor.map_comp]
      have hCombine₂ :
          (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
              (adjA.unit.app
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (c.2 ≫ a)).obj (A c.1))) ≫
            (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
              ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rA) =
          (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
            (adjA.unit.app
                ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (c.2 ≫ a)).obj (A c.1)) ≫
              (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map rA) := by
        rw [← Functor.map_comp]
      have hCombine₁' := hCombine₁
      dsimp only [adjA] at hCombine₁'
      have hUnitA'' := hUnitA'
      dsimp only [adjA] at hUnitA''
      have hCombine₂' := hCombine₂
      dsimp only [adjA] at hCombine₂'
      rw [hExpand₁]
      simp only [Category.assoc]
      rw [reassoc_of% hCombine₁', hUnitA'']
      rw [hExpand₂]
      simp only [Category.assoc]
      rw [reassoc_of% hCombine₂']
      have hHomUnitB := adjB.homEquiv_unit
      dsimp only [adjB] at hHomUnitB
      have hHomUnitA := adjA.homEquiv_unit
      dsimp only [adjA] at hHomUnitA
      have hHomUnitB' := hHomUnitB
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D ((c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b)).obj (A c.1))
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (c.2 ≫ a)).obj (A c.1)) rB
      have hHomUnitA' := hHomUnitA
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (c.2 ≫ a)).obj (A c.1))
        ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D c.2).obj (A c.1)) rA
      rw [reassoc_of% hHomUnitB'.symm]
      dsimp only [rB, c₁]
      rw [incomingRestriction_homEquiv.{v, u, w, t} D A b
        (show Incoming D j from ⟨c.1, c.2 ≫ a⟩)]
      rw [hHomUnitA'.symm]
      dsimp only [rA]
      rw [incomingRestriction_homEquiv.{v, u, w, t} D A a c]
      dsimp only [push]
      ext U x
      have hassoc := abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso_assoc.{v, u, w, t} D c.2 a b
      let cast := eqToIso (congrArg
        (fun f => (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D f).obj (A c.1))
        (Category.assoc c.2 a b))
      have hInv := congrArg (fun e => e.inv.app (A c.1)) hassoc
      have h := congrArg (fun q => cast.hom ≫ q ≫
        (abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).hom.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D c.2).obj (A c.1))) hInv
      simp only [cast,
        ] at h
      simpa [cast] using
        congrArg (fun q => q.hom x) (congrArg (fun q => q.hom.app U) h).symm
    _ = adjAB.homEquiv _ _
        ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b)).map
          (eqToHom (congrArg
            (fun f => (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D f).obj (A c.1))
            (Category.assoc c.2 a b))) ≫
          incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (a ≫ b) c) := rfl

private lemma productTransition_id (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (i : D.I) :
    (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
        (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i) ≫ productTransition.{v, u, w, t} D A (𝟙 i) =
      𝟙 (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i) := by
  apply Limits.Pi.hom_ext
  intro b
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  let b' : Incoming D i := ⟨b.1, b.2 ≫ 𝟙 i⟩
  have hb : b' = b := by cases b; simp [b']
  have hnat :
      (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i) ≫
        (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).map
          (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b') =
      Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b' ≫
        (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (b.2 ≫ 𝟙 i)).obj (A b.1)) :=
    ((abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.naturality
      (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b')).symm
  have hstep :
      (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i) ≫
        ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).map
          (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b') ≫
          incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (𝟙 i) b) =
      (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b' ≫
        (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (b.2 ≫ 𝟙 i)).obj (A b.1))) ≫
        incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (𝟙 i) b := by
    calc
      _ = ((abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
            (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i) ≫
          (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).map
            (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b')) ≫
            incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (𝟙 i) b :=
          (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
      _ = _ := congrArg (fun q => q ≫ incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (𝟙 i) b) hnat
  calc
    (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i) ≫
        productTransition.{v, u, w, t} D A (𝟙 i) ≫
          Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b =
        (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
          (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i) ≫
          ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).map
            (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b') ≫
            incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (𝟙 i) b) := by
      rw [productTransition_π]
    _ = _ := hstep
    _ = Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b' ≫
          ((abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 (𝟙 i)).inv.app (A b.1) ≫
            (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app
              ((abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).obj (A b.1))) := by
      rw [Category.assoc, incomingRestriction_id]
    _ = Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b := by
      rw [pushforwardCompId_inv_cancels]
      simp [hb]

private lemma productTransition_comp (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) {i j k : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) (b : j ⟶ k) :
    (abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).inv.app
        (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A k) ≫
      (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map (productTransition.{v, u, w, t} D A b) ≫
        productTransition.{v, u, w, t} D A a =
    productTransition.{v, u, w, t} D A (a ≫ b) := by
  apply Limits.Pi.hom_ext
  intro c
  simp only [Category.assoc, productTransition_π]
  simp only [← Category.assoc]
  conv_lhs =>
    arg 1
    rw [Category.assoc]
    arg 2
    rw [← Functor.map_comp]
  rw [productTransition_π]
  let c' : Incoming D k := ⟨c.1, (c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b⟩
  have hNat :
      (abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).inv.app
          (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A k) ≫
        (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
          ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b).map
            (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A k) c')) =
      (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b)).map
          (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A k) c') ≫
        (abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).inv.app
          (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A k c') := by
    simpa only [Functor.comp_map] using
      ((abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D a b).inv.naturality
        (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A k) c')).symm
  have hRestr := incomingRestriction_comp.{v, u, w, t} D A a b c
  rw [Functor.map_comp, reassoc_of% hNat]
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  dsimp only [c', incomingFactor] at hRestr ⊢
  rw [hRestr]
  simp only [← Category.assoc]
  rw [← Functor.map_comp]
  have hidx :
      (⟨c.1, (c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b⟩ : Incoming D k) = ⟨c.1, c.2 ≫ a ≫ b⟩ :=
    Sigma.ext rfl (heq_of_eq (Category.assoc c.2 a b))
  have hPi :
      Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A k)
          ⟨c.1, (c.2 ≫ a) ≫ b⟩ ≫
        eqToHom (congrArg (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A k) hidx) =
      Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A k) ⟨c.1, c.2 ≫ a ≫ b⟩ := by
    simpa [incomingFactor] using
      (Limits.Pi.π_comp_eqToHom (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A k) hidx)
  exact congrArg
    (fun q => (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D (a ≫ b)).map q ≫
      incomingRestriction.{v, u, w, t} D A (a ≫ b) c) hPi

/-- The system `G` of the source's proof: at each index the product
`∏_{b : k ⟶ i} f_{b,*} A_k`. -/
private noncomputable def productSystem (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D where
  obj i := productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i
  map a := productTransition.{v, u, w, t} D A a
  map_id i := productTransition_id.{v, u, w, t} D A i
  map_comp a b := productTransition_comp.{v, u, w, t} D A a b

/-- The component `F_i ⟶ f_{b,*} A_k` of the embedding, adjoint to
`f_b⁻¹ F_i ⟶ F_k ⟶ A_k`. -/
private noncomputable def envelopeComponent (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (F : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) (i : D.I) (b : Incoming D i) :
    F.obj i ⟶ incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D
      (injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F) i b :=
  letI := enoughInjectives.{v, u, w, t} D b.1
  (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).homEquiv (F.obj i)
    (injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F b.1)
    (F.map b.2 ≫ Injective.ι (F.obj b.1))

/-- The embedding `F_i ⟶ G_i` of the source's proof. -/
private noncomputable def envelopeMap (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (F : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) (i : D.I) :
    F.obj i ⟶ productObject.{v, u, w, t} D (injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F) i :=
  Limits.Pi.lift (envelopeComponent.{v, u, w, t} D F i)

private lemma pullbackIdIso_homEquiv_comp (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (i : D.I) (X Y : Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).homEquiv X
      Y
      ((abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app X ≫ f) =
    f ≫ (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app Y := by
  let adjId := Adjunction.id.ofNatIsoRight
    (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i)
  let adj := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)
  calc
    adj.homEquiv X Y ((abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app X ≫ f) =
    adj.homEquiv X ((𝟭 (Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t}))).obj X)
        ((Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq adj adjId).hom.app X) ≫
          (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).map f := by
      rw [abelianSheafPullbackIdIso, Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_right]
    _ = adjId.unit.app X ≫
        (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).map f := by
      rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_leftAdjointUniq_hom_app]
    _ = f ≫ (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app Y := by
      show (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app X ≫
          (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).map f = _
      exact (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.naturality f |>.symm

private lemma envelopeMap_naturality (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (F : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j) :
    (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D a).map (envelopeMap.{v, u, w, t} D F j) ≫
        productTransition.{v, u, w, t} D (injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F) a =
      F.map a ≫ envelopeMap.{v, u, w, t} D F i := by
  let A := injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F
  apply Limits.Pi.hom_ext
  intro b
  dsimp only [envelopeMap]
  rw [Category.assoc, productTransition_π, ← Category.assoc,
    ← Functor.map_comp, Limits.Pi.lift_comp_π]
  rw [Category.assoc, Limits.Pi.lift_comp_π]
  have : EnoughInjectives (Sheaf (D.J b.1) (Ab.{max u v w t})) :=
    enoughInjectives.{v, u, w, t} D b.1
  let adjA := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D a
  let adjB := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D b.2
  let c : Incoming D j := ⟨b.1, b.2 ≫ a⟩
  let adjC := abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D c.2
  let e := abelianSheafPushforwardCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 a
  let mB := envelopeComponent.{v, u, w, t} D F i b
  let mC := envelopeComponent.{v, u, w, t} D F j c
  have hfactor :
      ((abelianSheafPullbackCompIso.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 a).inv.app (F.obj j) ≫
        (abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).map (F.map a)) ≫
        F.map b.2 ≫ Injective.ι (F.obj b.1) =
      F.map (b.2 ≫ a) ≫ Injective.ι (F.obj b.1) := by
    simpa only [Category.assoc] using
      congrArg (fun q => q ≫ Injective.ι (F.obj b.1)) (F.map_comp b.2 a)
  have hright :
      (adjA.comp adjB).homEquiv (F.obj j) (A b.1)
        ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).map (F.map a) ≫
          F.map b.2 ≫ Injective.ι (F.obj b.1)) =
      adjA.homEquiv (F.obj j) (F.obj i) (F.map a) ≫
        (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map
          (envelopeComponent.{v, u, w, t} D F i b) := by
    dsimp only [A]
    rw [Adjunction.comp_homEquiv, Equiv.trans_apply]
    rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_left,
      Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_right]
    rfl
  have hmate := leftAdjointUniq_ofNatIsoRight_homEquiv_inv adjA adjB adjC e
    (X := F.obj j) (Y := A b.1)
    ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).map (F.map a) ≫
      F.map b.2 ≫ Injective.ι (F.obj b.1))
  apply (adjA.homEquiv (F.obj j) (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i b)).injective
  rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_left, Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_right]
  dsimp only [incomingFactor, A]
  rw [incomingRestriction, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]
  show mC ≫ e.inv.app (A b.1) =
    adjA.homEquiv (F.obj j) (F.obj i) (F.map a) ≫
      (abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D a).map mB
  dsimp only [mC, mB, envelopeComponent]
  rw [← hfactor]
  calc
    _ = (adjA.comp adjB).homEquiv (F.obj j) (A b.1)
          ((abelianSheafPullback.{v, u, w, t} D b.2).map (F.map a) ≫
            F.map b.2 ≫ Injective.ι (F.obj b.1)) := hmate
    _ = _ := hright

/-- The embedding of `F` into the product system of the source's proof. -/
private noncomputable def envelopeHom (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (F : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) :
    Hom.{v, u, w, t} F
      (productSystem.{v, u, w, t} D (injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F)) where
  app i := envelopeMap.{v, u, w, t} D F i
  naturality a := envelopeMap_naturality.{v, u, w, t} D F a

private lemma mono_envelopeMap (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (F : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) (i : D.I) :
    Mono (envelopeMap.{v, u, w, t} D F i) := by
  let A := injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F
  let b : Incoming D i := ⟨i, 𝟙 i⟩
  have : EnoughInjectives (Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) :=
    enoughInjectives.{v, u, w, t} D i
  have hπ : envelopeMap.{v, u, w, t} D F i ≫
      Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b =
      Injective.ι (F.obj i) ≫
        (abelianSheafPushforwardIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app (A i) := by
    have hmap : F.map (𝟙 i) =
        (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app (F.obj i) := by
      apply (cancel_epi
        ((abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app (F.obj i))).1
      calc
        (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app (F.obj i) ≫ F.map (𝟙 i) =
            𝟙 (F.obj i) := F.map_id i
        _ = (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).inv.app (F.obj i) ≫
              (abelianSheafPullbackIdIso.{v, u, w, t} D i).hom.app (F.obj i) := by simp
    dsimp only [A]
    show (Limits.Pi.lift (envelopeComponent.{v, u, w, t} D F i)) ≫
        Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D
          (injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F) i) b = _
    rw [Limits.Pi.lift_comp_π]
    show (abelianSheafAdjunction.{v, u, w, t} D (𝟙 i)).homEquiv
        (F.obj i) (injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F i)
        (F.map (𝟙 i) ≫ Injective.ι (F.obj i)) = _
    rw [hmap]
    exact pullbackIdIso_homEquiv_comp.{v, u, w, t} D i _ _ (Injective.ι (F.obj i))
  have : Mono (Injective.ι (F.obj i)) := Injective.ι_mono (F.obj i)
  have : Mono (envelopeMap.{v, u, w, t} D F i ≫
      Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b) := by
    rw [hπ]
    infer_instance
  exact mono_of_mono _ (Limits.Pi.π (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i) b)

private lemma injective_productObject (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w})
    (A : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Ab.{max u v w t})) (i : D.I)
    (hA : ∀ k, Injective (A k)) : Injective (productObject.{v, u, w, t} D A i) := by
  have : ∀ b : Incoming D i, Injective (incomingFactor.{v, u, w, t} D A i b) := by
    intro b
    let _ := hA b.1
    exact injective_abelianSheafPushforward.{v, u, w, t} D b.2 (A b.1)
  infer_instance

/-- **Stacks 0EXZ.** Every system of abelian sheaves on an inverse system of sites admits a
levelwise monomorphism to a system whose sheaf at every index is injective. -/
@[stacks 0EXZ "weak-system variant (Stacks 00VH finite coverings)"]
theorem exists_mono_to_pointwise_injective {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{v, u, w}}
    (F : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) :
    ∃ (G : AbelianSheafSystem.{v, u, w, t} D) (f : Hom.{v, u, w, t} F G),
      (∀ i, Mono (f.app i)) ∧ ∀ i, Injective (G.obj i) := by
  refine ⟨productSystem.{v, u, w, t} D (injectiveEnvelope.{v, u, w, t} D F),
    envelopeHom.{v, u, w, t} D F, fun i => mono_envelopeMap.{v, u, w, t} D F i, fun i => ?_⟩
  refine injective_productObject.{v, u, w, t} D _ i (fun k => ?_)
  let _ := enoughInjectives.{v, u, w, t} D k
  dsimp only [injectiveEnvelope]
  infer_instance

end AbelianSheafSystem

end InverseSystemOfFiniteSites

end

/-! # Sections of a colimit of sheaves on a colimit of sites

Let `D` be an inverse system of sites with finite coverings (Stacks 0A34): a cofiltered index
category `D.I`, for each `i` a site `(D.C i, D.J i)` all of whose coverings have a finite index
set, and for each `a : i ⟶ j` a continuous functor `D.u a : D.C j ⥤ D.C i`, compatibly with
composition. Let the functors `u i : D.C i ⥤ C` exhibit `C` as the colimit of the underlying
categories and let `K` be the coverings of `C` produced by Stacks 09YL, so that each `u i` defines
a morphism of sites `f_i : C → C_i` (Stacks 0A35).

Suppose given a sheaf of sets `F i` on each `(D.C i, D.J i)` together with, for every
`a : j ⟶ i`, a map `φ_a : f_a^{-1}F_i → F_j` of sheaves on `D.C j`, satisfying the cocycle
condition `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a`. These assemble into a diagram of sheaves on `C` with
value `f_i^{-1}F_i` at `i`, and the result of this file computes the sections of its colimit
`G = colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i` over an object coming from level `i`: for `X` an object of `D.C i`,
$$
G(u_i(X)) = \operatorname*{colim}_{a : j → i} F_j(u_a(X)),
$$
the colimit being over the (cofiltered) category of arrows into `i`, with transition maps the
`φ_b` read on sections. Since the index category of the colimit is cofiltered, the colimit of sets
on the right is described elementwise: the canonical maps into `G(u_i(X))` are jointly surjective,
and two sections at the same level with the same image become equal at some further level.

## Main results

* `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.sections_colimit_pullback_of_colimit`: the sections over `u_i(X)` of
  the colimit `colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i` of a system of sheaves on an inverse system of sites are the
  filtered colimit of the sections `F_j(u_a(X))` over the arrows `a : j ⟶ i` (Stacks 09YN).

## Implementation notes

The data (2) of the source and the colimit `G` are both phrased on the *pushforward* side, that
is through the adjunction `f_a^{-1} ⊣ f_{a,*}`, `f_{a,*} = (D.u a)^p` being restriction of
presheaves along `D.u a`:

* a map of sheaves `φ_a : f_a^{-1}F_i → F_j` is the same as a map `F_i → f_{a,*}F_j`, i.e. a
  morphism of presheaves `ψ a : (F i).val ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).val`, and its cocycle condition
  becomes `ψ (b ≫ a) = ψ a` followed by `ψ b`, an equality of maps on sections. On the pullback
  side the same equation needs the comparison isomorphism
  `f_{b ∘ a}^{-1} ≅ f_b^{-1} ∘ f_a^{-1}` (`CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafPullbackComp`), whereas on
  the pushforward side the corresponding comparison is the identity, the two composites being
  *equal* by `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.comp`. This is the same choice, for the same reason, as in
  the statement of Stacks 0A35.
* `G = colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i` is pinned by its universal property (`hG`) rather than by a
  construction, because the diagram `i ↦ f_i^{-1}F_i` is not available as a functor: the data
  given are the maps `φ_a` and equations between them, and turning them into a functor requires
  the comparison isomorphism above. A cocone on that diagram with vertex a sheaf `H` on `C` is,
  by the adjunction, exactly a family of morphisms of presheaves `g i : (F i).val ⟶ (u i).op ⋙
  H.val` compatible with the `ψ a` (`Hom_{Sh(C)}(f_i^{-1}F_i, H) = Hom_{PSh(C_i)}(F_i, u_i^p H)`),
  so `hι` says that `(G, ι)` is such a cocone and `hG` that it is the universal one.

Consequently no sheafification, no continuity instance and no `Functor.sheafPullback` occurs in
the statement: every map in it is a map on sections, and the only transports are along the
equalities of functors `D.u a ⋙ u j = u i` (`hu`) and `D.u (b ≫ a) = D.u a ⋙ D.u b`
(`InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.comp`), taken at an object. That each `u i` is a morphism of sites,
needed for `G` to deserve the name `colim f_i^{-1}F_i` and used in the proof through equation
(09YM), is not a hypothesis: it is a consequence of the hypotheses present, namely Stacks 0A35.

The family `ρ` of canonical maps `F_j(u_a(X)) → G(u_i(X))` is quantified over and pinned by `hρ`
to `ι j` followed by the identification `u_j(u_a(X)) = u_i(X)`; this only avoids writing that
composite four times, `∀ ρ, ρ = e → P ρ` and `P e` being the same statement. Likewise the
conclusion is the elementwise description of a filtered colimit of sets rather than an
`IsColimit`, for the same reason as in Stacks 0A35: the diagram over the category of arrows into
`i` is again not available as a functor. Separatedness is stated for two sections at the *same*
level, which together with joint surjectivity and `hι` gives the general case, the index category
being cofiltered.

That `C` is the colimit of the `D.C i` is spelled out as `hobj`, `hhom` and `hhom_inj`, and the
coverings of `C` as `hK`, exactly as in the statement of Stacks 09YL, whose conclusion supplies
them. The source's `\mathcal F` is `G` here, the letter `F` being taken by the family `F i` of the
source's `\mathcal F_i`.

On faithfulness:
* No hypothesis is dead: `hu`, `hobj`, `hhom`, `hhom_inj` say that `u` exhibits `C` as the colimit
  of the system and `hK` says which families are coverings of `C`, which is what makes the `u i`
  morphisms of sites and hence the left-hand side a colimit of sections; `hu` moreover enters the
  conclusion itself, through the identification `u_j(u_a(X)) = u_i(X)` defining `ρ`. `ψ` and `hψ`
  are the source's data (2) and its cocycle condition, and `ι`, `hι`, `hG` are the equation
  `G = colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i`.
* The data is the source's: the sites, the cofiltered index category and the finiteness of the
  coverings are those of `D`, whose transition functors are its continuous `D.u a`; the sheaves are
  sheaves of sets on the `(D.C i, D.J i)` and on `C` with the topology generated by the coverings
  of Stacks 09YL.
* The canonical maps are pinned, not merely asserted to exist: `ρ` by `hρ`, the colimit `G` by
  `hι` and `hG` up to the unique isomorphism the universal property allows, and the transition
  maps of the colimit on the left by `ψ`.
* The instantiation is not degenerate: take `D.I` the one-object category, `D.C` a single small
  category with the trivial topology, `D.u` the identity functor, `C` that category and `u` the
  identity functor; then `hu`–`hK` hold, `f_i^{-1}` is the identity, `G = F i` with `ι` the
  identity satisfies `hι` and `hG`, and the conclusion says that a one-term filtered colimit of
  sets is what it is.

## References

* [Stacks 09YN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09YN)
-/

namespace CategoryTheory.Sites.InverseSystem

section

universe u₁ u₂ w
open CategoryTheory Opposite

namespace Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections

@[expose] public section

/-- The subpresheaf of `G` whose sections over `V` are the restrictions, along the morphisms
`V ⟶ u_i(Y)` of `C`, of the sections of `G` in the image of `ι i`. It is the subpresheaf of `G`
generated by the images of the maps `ι i`. -/
private def imageSubfunctor {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C]
    {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}}
    {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C} {K : Precoverage C} {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    {G : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)} (ι : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ G.obj) :
    Subfunctor G.obj
    where
  obj U :=
    {s |
      ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (p : U.unop ⟶ (u i).obj Y) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op Y)),
        s = G.obj.map p.op ((ι i).app (op Y) x)}
  map := by
    rintro U V f s ⟨i, Y, p, x, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨i, Y, f.unop ≫ p, x, ?_⟩
    rw [op_comp, Quiver.Hom.op_unop, Functor.map_comp_apply]

/-- A section in the image of `ι i` lies in `imageSubfunctor ι`. -/
private lemma mem_imageSubfunctor {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C]
    {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}} {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C} {K : Precoverage C}
    {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)} {G : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)}
    (ι : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ G.obj) (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op Y)) :
    (ι i).app (op Y) x ∈ (imageSubfunctor ι).obj (op ((u i).obj Y)) :=
  ⟨i, Y, 𝟙 _, x, by simp⟩

/-- The factorisation of `ι i` through a subfunctor `A` of `G` containing its image. -/
private def liftSubfunctor {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C]
    {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}}
    {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C} {K : Precoverage C} {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    {G : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)} (ι : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ G.obj)
    (A : Subfunctor G.obj)
    (hmem :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (Y : (D.C i)ᵒᵖ) (x : (F i).obj.obj Y), (ι i).app Y x ∈ A.obj ((u i).op.obj Y))
    (i : D.I) : (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ A.toFunctor
    where
  app Y := ↾fun x => ⟨(ι i).app Y x, hmem i Y x⟩
  naturality := by
    intro Y Z f
    apply ConcreteCategory.hom_ext
    intro x
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    exact NatTrans.naturality_apply (ι i) f x

/-- Transport of sections along an equality of objects is injective. -/
private lemma map_eqToHom_injective {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w) {U V : Cᵒᵖ}
    (e : U = V) : Function.Injective (P.map (eqToHom e)) := by
  subst e
  intro x y hxy
  simpa using hxy

/-- A section of `G` over `V` **comes from a level** if `V` is the image `u_k(Y)` of an object `Y`
at some level `k` and the section is the image under `ι k` of a section of `F k` over `Y`. The
content of Stacks 09YN is that every section of `G` comes from a level, in a way compatible with a
chosen presentation of the object it lives over. -/
private def ComesFromLevel {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C]
    {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}}
    {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C} {K : Precoverage C} {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    {G : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)} (ι : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ G.obj) (V : C)
    (s : G.obj.obj (op V)) : Prop :=
  ∃ (k : D.I) (Y : D.C k) (h : (u k).obj Y = V) (t : (F k).obj.obj (op Y)),
    G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op h)) ((ι k).app (op Y) t) = s

/-- **The sheaf of `K`-closed relations to `Z`.** A section over `V` assigns to every object
`(W, a : W ⟶ V)` of `Over V` and every morphism `b : W ⟶ Z` a `K`-closed sieve on `W`, naturally
in `(W, a)`.

This is the exponential `Ω^{yZ}` of the subobject classifier `Ω` of the topos of sheaves on `C`:
`Ω` is `CategoryTheory.Functor.closedSieves`, a sheaf by `CategoryTheory.classifier_isSheaf`, and
the internal hom `CategoryTheory.presheafHom` of presheaves into a sheaf is again a sheaf by
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.IsSheaf.hom`. Since `C` is small it is `Type w`-valued, so the universal
property of `G = colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i` applies to it. -/
private lemma isSheaf_presheafHom_closedSieves {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (K : Precoverage C)
    (Z : C) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf K.toGrothendieck
      (presheafHom (yoneda.obj Z) (Functor.closedSieves K.toGrothendieck).toFunctor) :=
  Presheaf.IsSheaf.hom (yoneda.obj Z) (Functor.closedSieves K.toGrothendieck).toFunctor
    ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).2 (classifier_isSheaf K.toGrothendieck))

private def relSheaf {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (K : Precoverage C) (Z : C) :
    Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w) :=
  ⟨presheafHom (yoneda.obj Z) (Functor.closedSieves K.toGrothendieck).toFunctor,
    isSheaf_presheafHom_closedSieves K Z⟩

/-- Two sections **agree at a level along `f` and `h`**: for `s` a section of `F k` over `B`, `t` a
section of `F j` over `A` and morphisms `f : W ⟶ u_k(B)`, `h : W ⟶ u_j(A)` of `C`, there are
`e : n ⟶ k`, `d : n ⟶ j`, an object `W'` of `D.C n`, morphisms `f' : W' ⟶ u_e(B)`,
`h' : W' ⟶ u_d(A)` of `D.C n` and a morphism `p : W ⟶ u_n(W')` of `C` through which `f` and `h`
factor as the images of `f'` and `h'`, such that the restrictions of `ψ_e s` along `f'` and of
`ψ_d t` along `h'` agree.

The factorisation is through an arbitrary morphism `p` of `C` rather than through an
identification `u_n(W') = W`, which is what makes the relation stable under precomposition
(`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.AgreeAtLevel.comp`) with no descent argument at all, hence
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.agreeSieve` a sieve whose assignment is natural. -/
private def AgreeAtLevel {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}}
    {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C} (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj) {j : D.I} {A : D.C j}
    (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C}
    (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B) (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A) : Prop :=
  ∃ (n : D.I) (e : n ⟶ k) (d : n ⟶ j) (W' : D.C n) (p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W') (f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B)
    (h' : W' ⟶ (D.u d).obj A),
    f = p ≫ (u n).map f' ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu e) B) ∧
      h = p ≫ (u n).map h' ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu d) A) ∧
      (F n).obj.map f'.op ((ψ e).app (op B) s) = (F n).obj.map h'.op ((ψ d).app (op A) t)

/-- Agreement at a level is stable under precomposition: compose the factorisation with the
morphism. -/
private lemma AgreeAtLevel.comp {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C]
    {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}} {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C}
    {hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j} {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    {ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj} {j : D.I} {A : D.C j}
    {t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)} {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} {s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)} {W : C}
    {f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B} {h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A} (hfh : AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s f h) {W₀ : C}
    (g : W₀ ⟶ W) : AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s (g ≫ f) (g ≫ h) := by
  obtain ⟨n, e, d, W', p, f', h', hf, hh, heq⟩ := hfh
  exact ⟨n, e, d, W', g ≫ p, f', h', by rw [hf, Category.assoc], by rw [hh, Category.assoc], heq⟩

/-- The sieve of the morphisms `c` along which `s` and `t` agree at a level, that is, such that
they agree at a level along `c ≫ f` and `c ≫ h`. -/
private def agreeSieve {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}}
    {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C} (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj) {j : D.I} {A : D.C j}
    (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C}
    (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B) (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A) : Sieve W
    where
  arrows := fun {_} c => AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s (c ≫ f) (c ≫ h)
  downward_closed := by
    intro W₁ W₂ c hc g
    simpa only [Category.assoc] using hc.comp g

/-- Membership in the sieve of agreement at a level. -/
private lemma agreeSieve_apply {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C]
    {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}} {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C}
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j) {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj) {j : D.I} {A : D.C j}
    (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C}
    (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B) (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A) {W₁ : C} (c : W₁ ⟶ W) :
    agreeSieve hu ψ t s f h c ↔ AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s (c ≫ f) (c ≫ h) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The sieve of agreement at a level pulls back to the sieve of agreement along the composites:
the assignment `f, h ↦ agreeSieve f h` is natural. -/
private lemma agreeSieve_pullback {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C]
    {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}} {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C}
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j) {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj) {j : D.I} {A : D.C j}
    (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C}
    (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B) (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A) {W₀ : C} (g : W₀ ⟶ W) :
    (agreeSieve hu ψ t s f h).pullback g = agreeSieve hu ψ t s (g ≫ f) (g ≫ h) := by
  ext W₁ c
  rw [Sieve.pullback_apply, agreeSieve_apply, agreeSieve_apply, Category.assoc, Category.assoc]

/-- A section agrees with itself at its own level, along the identity. This is the element of the
sieve of agreement that the separatedness argument transports from `t` to `t'`. -/
private lemma agreeAtLevel_self {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C]
    {D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}} {u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C}
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j) {F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w)}
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj) {j : D.I} {A : D.C j}
    (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) : AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t t (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) := by
  refine
      ⟨j, 𝟙 j, 𝟙 j, (D.u (𝟙 j)).obj A, eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu (𝟙 j)) A).symm, 𝟙 _, 𝟙 _, ?_,
        ?_, rfl⟩ <;>
    simp

/-- Membership in a presieve transported along an equality of objects: the transport of `P` along
`h : A = B` contains the transport `f ≫ eqToHom h` of every member `f` of `P`. This is how the
description `hK` of the coverings of `C`, whose right-hand side carries such a transport, is read
off a member of the covering it comes from. -/
private lemma mem_of_eq_cast {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] {A B : C} (h : A = B) {P : Presieve A}
    {R : Presieve B} (hR : R = h ▸ P) {W : C} (f : W ⟶ A) (hf : P f) : R (f ≫ eqToHom h) := by
  subst h
  rw [eqToHom_refl, Category.comp_id, hR]
  exact hf

/-- A finite family of arrows generating a covering sieve still does after its common target is
transported along an equality of objects. -/
private lemma ofArrows_comp_eqToHom_mem_toPrecoverage {E : Type w} [SmallCategory E]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology E) {V V' : E} (h : V = V') {α : Type} (B : α → E) (g : ∀ r, B r ⟶ V)
    (hg : Presieve.ofArrows B g ∈ J.toPrecoverage V) :
    Presieve.ofArrows B (fun r => g r ≫ eqToHom h) ∈ J.toPrecoverage V' := by
  subst h
  simpa using hg

section

variable {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w})
  (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
  (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
  (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
  (hhom :
    ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
      ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
        (u j).map g =
          eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
  (hhom_inj :
    ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
      (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
  (K : Precoverage C)
  (hK :
    ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
      R ∈ K X ↔
        ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
          S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
  (F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w))
  (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj)
  (hψ :
    ∀ {i j k : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (b : k ⟶ j) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
      (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) x =
        (F k).obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp b a) V).symm))
          ((ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
  (G : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)) (ι : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ G.obj)
  (hι :
    ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
      (ι i).app (op V) x =
        G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
          ((ι j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
  (hG :
    ∀ (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)) (g : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj),
      (∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
          (g i).app (op V) x =
            H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
              ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x))) →
        ∃! h : G ⟶ H,
          ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
            (g i).app (op V) x = h.hom.app (op ((u i).obj V)) ((ι i).app (op V) x))

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK in
/-- The coverings of `C` of Stacks 09YL are a coverage: the fibre products of the members of a
covering along any morphism exist and form a covering, so a covering of the target pulls back to
one of the source. This is the part of the conclusion of Stacks 09YL that this file consumes. -/
private lemma exists_coverage_toPrecoverage_eq : ∃ Cov : Coverage C, Cov.toPrecoverage = K := by
  obtain ⟨K', hK', -, -, hPB, hstab⟩ :=
    InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.exists_precoverage_of_colimit D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj
  obtain rfl : K' = K :=
    Precoverage.ext (funext fun X => Set.ext fun R => (hK' X R).trans (hK X R).symm)
  refine ⟨{ __ := K', pullback := fun {X Y} f S hS => ?_ }, rfl⟩
  have := hPB.hasPullbacks_of_mem f hS
  exact ⟨S.pullbackArrows f, hstab X Y f S hS, Presieve.FactorsThruAlong.pullbackArrows f S⟩

/-- Finitely many levels admit a common level below all of them, the index category being
cofiltered. -/
private lemma exists_hom_forall {α : Type*} [Finite α] (lev : α → D.I) :
    ∃ m : D.I, ∀ r : α, Nonempty (m ⟶ lev r) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := IsCofiltered.inf_objs_exists (C := D.I) (Set.finite_range lev).toFinset
  exact ⟨m, fun r => hm (by simp)⟩

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK in
/-- The three conditions of Stacks 00VH for the coverings of `C`, read off the conclusion of
Stacks 09YL for the precoverage `K` that `hK` pins down: a family given by an isomorphism is a
covering, coverings are stable under refinement by coverings, and the fibre products of a covering
along an arbitrary morphism exist and form a covering. -/
lemma hasIsos_and_bind_and_pullbackArrows :
    K.HasIsos ∧
      (∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X) (T : ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (f : Y ⟶ X), R f → Presieve Y),
        R ∈ K X → (∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (f : Y ⟶ X) (hf : R f), T f hf ∈ K Y) → R.bind T ∈ K X) ∧
      ∃ _ : K.HasPullbacks,
        ∀ (X Y : C) (f : Y ⟶ X) (R : Presieve X) [R.HasPullbacks f],
          R ∈ K X → R.pullbackArrows f ∈ K Y := by
  obtain ⟨K', hK', hIso, hbind, hPB, hstab⟩ :=
    InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.exists_precoverage_of_colimit D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj
  obtain rfl : K' = K :=
    Precoverage.ext (funext fun X => Set.ext fun R => (hK' X R).trans (hK X R).symm)
  exact ⟨hIso, hbind, hPB, hstab⟩

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK in
/-- **Every covering sieve of `C` is refined by a covering.** The coverings of Stacks 09YL satisfy
the three conditions of Stacks 00VH, so the Grothendieck topology they generate contains no
covering sieves beyond those they force: a sieve is covering exactly when some covering refines it.

This is what turns a local statement about `K.toGrothendieck` back into a statement about a
*finite* covering coming from a level, which is the only form the sheaves `F i` can consume. -/
private lemma exists_mem_le_of_mem_toGrothendieck {X : C} (S : Sieve X)
    (hS : S ∈ K.toGrothendieck X) : ∃ R ∈ K X, R ≤ S.arrows := by
  obtain ⟨hIso, hbind, hPBinst, hstab⟩ :=
    hasIsos_and_bind_and_pullbackArrows D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK
  rw [Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff] at hS
  induction hS with
  | of Y R hR => exact ⟨R, hR, Sieve.le_generate R⟩
  | top Y => exact ⟨Presieve.singleton (𝟙 Y), hIso.mem_coverings_of_isIso (𝟙 Y), by simp⟩
  | pullback Y S _ Z f ih =>
    obtain ⟨R, hR, hle⟩ := ih
    have := hPBinst.hasPullbacks_of_mem f hR
    refine ⟨R.pullbackArrows f, hstab _ _ f R hR, ?_⟩
    intro W g hg
    obtain ⟨T, i, h, hh, hcomm⟩ := Presieve.FactorsThruAlong.pullbackArrows f R hg
    rw [Sieve.pullback_apply, ← hcomm]
    have hh' : S.arrows h := by
      apply hle; exact hh
    exact S.downward_closed hh' i
  | transitive Y S R _ _ ihS ihSR =>
    obtain ⟨R₀, hR₀, hle⟩ := ihS
    have key : ∀ (Z : C) (g : Z ⟶ Y), R₀ g → ∃ T, T ∈ K Z ∧ T ≤ (R.pullback g).arrows :=
      fun Z g hg => by
      have hgS : S.arrows g := by
        apply hle; exact hg
      obtain ⟨T, hT, hT'⟩ := ihSR hgS
      exact ⟨T, hT, hT'⟩
    choose T hT hT' using key
    refine ⟨R₀.bind fun Z g hg => T Z g hg, hbind Y R₀ _ hR₀ fun Z g hg => hT Z g hg, ?_⟩
    rintro Z h ⟨W, g, p, hp, hg, rfl⟩
    rw [← Sieve.pullback_apply]
    apply hT' W p hp
    exact hg

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK hι hG in
/-- **Every section of `G = colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i` is a gluing of restrictions of sections in the
image of the maps `ι i`**: it lies in the closure of `imageSubfunctor ι` under restriction and
gluing along the coverings of `K` (`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.SubsheafClosure`).

That closure is a subsheaf of `G`, because `G` is a sheaf and `K` is a coverage, and the maps
`ι i` factor through it compatibly with the `ψ a`; so the universal property of `G` gives a map
from `G` to it whose composite with the inclusion is compatible with the `ι i`, and the identity of
`G` is another such map, so the two agree and the subsheaf is all of `G`.

Apart from the coverage property of `K`, only the universal property of `G` is used. -/
private lemma subsheafClosure_imageSubfunctor (V : C) (s : G.obj.obj (op V)) :
    K.SubsheafClosure (fun Z => (imageSubfunctor ι).obj (op Z)) V s := by
  have hGs : Presieve.IsSheaf K.toGrothendieck G.obj :=
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).1 G.property
  -- the `K`-sheafification of the image family, a subsheaf of `G`
  have hsh :
    Presieve.IsSheaf K.toGrothendieck
      (K.subsheafify (fun Z => (imageSubfunctor ι).obj (op Z))).toFunctor := by
    obtain ⟨Cov, hCov⟩ := exists_coverage_toPrecoverage_eq D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK
    have hCovG : Cov.toGrothendieck = K.toGrothendieck := by
      rw [← Coverage.toGrothendieck_toPrecoverage, hCov]
    have key :
      Presieve.IsSheaf Cov.toGrothendieck
        (K.subsheafify (fun Z => (imageSubfunctor ι).obj (op Z))).toFunctor := by
      rw [Presieve.isSheaf_coverage]
      intro X R hR
      have hR' : R ∈ K X := by
        rw [← hCov]; exact hR
      exact
        Precoverage.isSheafFor_subsheafify _ hR'
          ((Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate R).2
            (hGs _ (Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hR')))
    rwa [hCovG] at key
  have hmem :
    ∀ (i : D.I) (Y : (D.C i)ᵒᵖ) (x : (F i).obj.obj Y),
      (ι i).app Y x ∈
        (K.subsheafify (fun Z => (imageSubfunctor ι).obj (op Z))).obj ((u i).op.obj Y) :=
    fun i Y x => Precoverage.SubsheafClosure.base (mem_imageSubfunctor ι i Y.unop x)
  -- the maps `ι i` factor through that subsheaf, compatibly with the `ψ a`
  obtain ⟨h, hh, -⟩ :=
    hG ⟨_, (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).2 hsh⟩ (liftSubfunctor ι _ hmem)
      (by
        intro i j a W x
        refine Subtype.ext ?_
        exact hι a W x)
  obtain ⟨h₀, -, huniq⟩ := hG G ι hι
  -- the composite `G ⟶ A ⟶ G` is compatible with the `ι i`, hence is the identity of `G`
  have e₁ :
    (ObjectProperty.homMk (h.hom ≫ (K.subsheafify (fun Z => (imageSubfunctor ι).obj (op Z))).ι) :
        G ⟶ G) =
      h₀ :=
    huniq _ fun i W x => congrArg Subtype.val (hh i W x)
  have e₂ : (𝟙 G : G ⟶ G) = h₀ := huniq _ fun _ _ _ => rfl
  have hk :
    (𝟙 G.obj : G.obj ⟶ G.obj) =
      h.hom ≫ (K.subsheafify (fun Z => (imageSubfunctor ι).obj (op Z))).ι :=
    congrArg (fun f : G ⟶ G => f.hom) (e₂.trans e₁.symm)
  have hs : s = (h.hom.app (op V) s).1 := by
    simpa using congrArg (fun f : G.obj ⟶ G.obj => f.app (op V) s) hk
  have h2 := (h.hom.app (op V) s).2
  rw [← hs] at h2
  exact h2

include hu hhom in
/-- **A morphism of `C` between presented objects is the image of a morphism at a level.** A
morphism `p : u_i(X) ⟶ u_k(Y)` of `C` is, after transporting along the identifications
`u_m(u_c(X)) = u_i(X)` and `u_m(u_d(Y)) = u_k(Y)`, the image under `u_m` of a morphism
`g : u_c(X) ⟶ u_d(Y)` of `D.C m`, for some level `m` with arrows `c : m ⟶ i` and `d : m ⟶ k`.

This is `hhom` with the two levels no longer required to be equal: the levels `i` and `k` are first
pushed to a common level, which is where `p` becomes a morphism between two objects of one `D.C n`
and `hhom` applies. It is the descent step that every argument in this file performs — on the
morphism a section is restricted along (`exists_level_of_hom`), and on the morphism `p` that a
witness of `AgreeAtLevel` factors through — so it is stated once here. -/
private lemma exists_level_hom_of_hom (i : D.I) (X : D.C i) (k : D.I) (Y : D.C k)
    (p : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u k).obj Y) :
    ∃ (m : D.I) (c : m ⟶ i) (d : m ⟶ k) (g : (D.u c).obj X ⟶ (D.u d).obj Y),
      (u m).map g =
        eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu c) X) ≫ p ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu d) Y).symm := by
  -- a level `n` below both `i` and `k`, where `p` becomes a morphism of a single `D.C n`
  obtain ⟨n, c, d, -⟩ := IsCofilteredOrEmpty.cone_objs i k
  -- the level `m` at which that morphism lives
  obtain ⟨m, e, g, hg⟩ :=
    hhom n ((D.u c).obj X) ((D.u d).obj Y)
      (eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu c) X) ≫ p ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu d) Y).symm)
  have hX : (D.u (e ≫ c)).obj X = (D.u e).obj ((D.u c).obj X) := Functor.congr_obj (D.comp e c) X
  have hY : (D.u (e ≫ d)).obj Y = (D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj Y) := Functor.congr_obj (D.comp e d) Y
  refine ⟨m, e ≫ c, e ≫ d, eqToHom hX ≫ g ≫ eqToHom hY.symm, ?_⟩
  simp [hg, eqToHom_map]

include hu hobj hhom in
/-- **A section agrees with itself at a level along an arbitrary morphism of `C`.** The morphism
`f : W ⟶ u_k(B)` is factored through a level by presenting `W` as `u_l(W₀)` and descending `f`
with `exists_level_hom_of_hom`; the equation of sections is then an identity.

This is `agreeAtLevel_self`, which is the case `f = 𝟙`, for an arbitrary `f`. It is the reflexivity
that makes the assignment `s ↦ agreeSieve hu ψ t s` invariant under the two moves relating germs of
the same section of `G` — restriction along a morphism of `D.C k` and passage from `s` to `ψ_a s` —
each of those being a comparison of two germs along a *single* morphism, hence reflexivity composed
with transitivity of agreement at a level. -/
private lemma agreeAtLevel_refl {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C}
    (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B) : AgreeAtLevel hu ψ s s f f := by
  obtain ⟨l, W₀, rfl⟩ := hobj W
  obtain ⟨n, c, e, g, hg⟩ := exists_level_hom_of_hom D u hu hhom l W₀ k B f
  refine ⟨n, e, e, (D.u c).obj W₀, eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu c) W₀).symm, g, g, ?_, ?_, rfl⟩
  · rw [hg]; simp
  · rw [hg]; simp

include hu hhom hι in
/-- **A section pulled back along a morphism of `C` comes from a level.** Let `X` be an object of
`D.C i`, let `p : u_i(X) ⟶ u_k(Y)` be a morphism of `C` and let `x` be a section of `F k` over `Y`.
Then the restriction of `ι k x` along `p` is `ι m` of a section of `F m` over `u_a(X)` for some
`a : m ⟶ i`.

Since `C` is the colimit of the `D.C i`, the morphism `p` is the image of a morphism at some level
`m` below both `i` and `k`, and there the section `x` becomes `ψ x`. -/
private lemma exists_level_of_hom (i : D.I) (X : D.C i) (k : D.I) (Y : D.C k)
    (p : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u k).obj Y) (x : (F k).obj.obj (op Y)) :
    ∃ (m : D.I) (a : m ⟶ i) (t : (F m).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X))),
      G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X)))
          ((ι m).app (op ((D.u a).obj X)) t) =
        G.obj.map p.op ((ι k).app (op Y) x) := by
  obtain ⟨m, c, d, g, hg⟩ := exists_level_hom_of_hom D u hu hhom i X k Y p
  -- the identity of morphisms recorded by `hg`, read in `Cᵒᵖ`
  have key :
    ((u m).map g).op ≫ eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu c) X)) =
      eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu d) Y)) ≫ p.op := by
    rw [hg]
    simp
  refine ⟨m, c, (F m).obj.map g.op ((ψ d).app (op Y) x), ?_⟩
  rw [hι d Y x, NatTrans.naturality_apply (ι m) g.op ((ψ d).app (op Y) x)]
  simp only [Functor.comp_map, Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op]
  rw [← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, key]

include hu hobj hhom hι in
/-- Coming from a level is preserved by restriction along an arbitrary morphism of `C`: this is
`exists_level_of_hom` after presenting the source of the morphism as `u_l(W)`. -/
private lemma comesFromLevel_of_map (V : C) (k : D.I) (Y : D.C k) (p : V ⟶ (u k).obj Y)
    (x : (F k).obj.obj (op Y)) : ComesFromLevel ι V (G.obj.map p.op ((ι k).app (op Y) x)) := by
  obtain ⟨l, W, rfl⟩ := hobj V
  obtain ⟨m, b, t, hb⟩ := exists_level_of_hom D u hu hhom K F ψ G ι hι l W k Y p x
  exact ⟨m, (D.u b).obj W, Functor.congr_obj (hu b) W, t, hb⟩

include hu hhom hι in
/-- **A section that comes from a level, presented over a chosen object.** If a section of `G` over
`u_{i₀}(Y₀)` comes from a level, then it is `ι m` of a section of `F m` over `(D.u e).obj Y₀` for
some `e : m ⟶ i₀` — that is, the level can be chosen below `i₀` and the object to be the transport
of the *given* presentation `Y₀`, not the one the section happens to carry.

Two presentations `u_k(Y) = u_{i₀}(Y₀)` of one object of `C` need not be related by any morphism at
level `k` or `i₀`, so this is not a formal manipulation; it is `exists_level_of_hom` applied to the
identity of `u_{i₀}(Y₀)`, read as a morphism `u_{i₀}(Y₀) ⟶ u_k(Y)`. In particular no lemma
matching two presentations by an *isomorphism* at a common level is needed for this. -/
private lemma exists_level_of_comesFromLevel (i₀ : D.I) (Y₀ : D.C i₀)
    (s : G.obj.obj (op ((u i₀).obj Y₀))) (hs : ComesFromLevel ι ((u i₀).obj Y₀) s) :
    ∃ (m : D.I) (e : m ⟶ i₀) (t : (F m).obj.obj (op ((D.u e).obj Y₀))),
      G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu e) Y₀)))
          ((ι m).app (op ((D.u e).obj Y₀)) t) =
        s := by
  obtain ⟨k, Y, h, w, hw⟩ := hs
  obtain ⟨m, e, t, ht⟩ := exists_level_of_hom D u hu hhom K F ψ G ι hι i₀ Y₀ k Y (eqToHom h.symm) w
  refine ⟨m, e, t, ?_⟩
  rw [ht, ← hw, eqToHom_op]

include hK in
/-- **A covering of `C` is the image of a finite family of arrows at a level.** This is the
description `hK` of the coverings of Stacks 09YL, with the finite presieve replaced by the finite
family of arrows it indexes; finiteness of the family is not carried in the conclusion because
`Precoverage.ofArrows_mem_finite` recovers it from `Finite α`.

It is the first step of any descent along a covering of `C`: the level `i₀` is where the covering
lives, and `α` is the finite index set whose members' levels a cone
(`CategoryTheory.IsCofiltered.wideCospan`) pushes to one. -/
private lemma exists_finite_arrows_of_mem (Z : C) (R : Presieve Z) (hR : R ∈ K Z) :
    ∃ (i₀ : D.I) (Y₀ : D.C i₀) (h : (u i₀).obj Y₀ = Z) (α : Type w) (_ : Finite α) (B : α → D.C i₀)
      (g : ∀ p, B p ⟶ Y₀),
      Presieve.ofArrows B g ∈ (D.J i₀).toPrecoverage Y₀ ∧
        R = h ▸ (Presieve.ofArrows B g).map (u i₀) := by
  obtain ⟨i₀, Y₀, h, S, hS, hfin, rfl⟩ := (hK Z R).1 hR
  obtain ⟨α, hα, B, g, rfl⟩ := StacksWeakAux.exists_ofArrows_of_mem_finite S hfin
  exact ⟨i₀, Y₀, h, α, hα, B, g, hS, rfl⟩

/-- **The transition functors preserve finite coverings.** A finite covering of `Y` in `D.C i₀` is
carried by `D.u a`, for `a : m ⟶ i₀`, to a finite covering of `(D.u a).obj Y` in `D.C m`.

This is Stacks 00WV (1) for the morphism of sites `f_a`, which Situation 0A34 records as
`InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.coverPreserving`; finiteness travels with the covering because it is a
conjunct of that hypothesis, and it is needed because the coverings of `C` of Stacks 09YL are
images of *finite* coverings. -/
private lemma map_mem_toPrecoverage_and_finite {i₀ m : D.I} (a : m ⟶ i₀) {Y : D.C i₀}
    {S : Presieve Y} (hS : S ∈ (D.J i₀).toPrecoverage Y)
    (hfin : S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i₀) Y) :
    S.map (D.u a) ∈ (D.J m).toPrecoverage ((D.u a).obj Y) ∧
      S.map (D.u a) ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C m) ((D.u a).obj Y) :=
  D.coverPreserving a Y ⟨hS, hfin⟩

/-- **Two parallel arrows of the index category are equalized from below.** For `f g : i₀ ⟶ j₀`
there is `b : m ⟶ i₀` with both composites `b ≫ f` and `b ≫ g` equal to one arrow `c : m ⟶ j₀`.

This is `CategoryTheory.IsCofiltered.eq_condition`; the descent of germs makes the arrows of two
factorisations equal before the sections they transport can be compared. -/
private lemma exists_hom_eq_pair {i₀ j₀ : D.I} (f g : i₀ ⟶ j₀) :
    ∃ (m : D.I) (b : m ⟶ i₀) (c : m ⟶ j₀), b ≫ f = c ∧ b ≫ g = c :=
  ⟨_, _, _, rfl, (IsCofiltered.eq_condition f g).symm⟩

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK in
/-- **A covering sieve of a presented object is refined by a finite covering at a level.** For `X`
an object of `D.C i` and `S` a covering sieve of `u_i(X)` for the topology generated by the
coverings of Stacks 09YL, there are an arrow `a : m ⟶ i` and a finite covering
`{g_r : B_r ⟶ u_a(X)}` of `D.C m` each of whose members maps into `S`.

This is the descent of a covering of `C` to a single level, and it is what makes the sheaf property
of the `F i` available to a statement that holds locally on `C`. -/
private lemma exists_level_covering (i : D.I) (X : D.C i) (S : Sieve ((u i).obj X))
    (hS : S ∈ K.toGrothendieck ((u i).obj X)) :
    ∃ (m : D.I) (a : m ⟶ i) (α : Type) (_ : Finite α) (B : α → D.C m) (g :
      ∀ r, B r ⟶ (D.u a).obj X),
      Presieve.ofArrows B g ∈ (D.J m).toPrecoverage ((D.u a).obj X) ∧
        ∀ r, S.arrows ((u m).map (g r) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X)) := by
  obtain ⟨R, hR, hRS⟩ := exists_mem_le_of_mem_toGrothendieck D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK S hS
  obtain ⟨i₀, Y₀, hY₀, α₀, hα₀, B₀, g₀, hS₀, hReq⟩ :=
    exists_finite_arrows_of_mem D u K hK ((u i).obj X) R hR
  have := hα₀
  have hS₀fin : Presieve.ofArrows B₀ g₀ ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i₀) Y₀ :=
    Precoverage.ofArrows_mem_finite B₀ g₀
  obtain ⟨n, c, d, -⟩ := IsCofilteredOrEmpty.cone_objs i i₀
  -- the identity of `u_i(X) = u_{i₀}(Y₀)`, read at the level `n` and descended to a level `m`
  have hnc : (u n).obj ((D.u c).obj X) = (u i).obj X := Functor.congr_obj (hu c) X
  have hnd : (u n).obj ((D.u d).obj Y₀) = (u i₀).obj Y₀ := Functor.congr_obj (hu d) Y₀
  have hn : (u n).obj ((D.u c).obj X) = (u n).obj ((D.u d).obj Y₀) := by rw [hnc, hnd, hY₀]
  obtain ⟨m, e, ξ, hξ⟩ := hhom n ((D.u c).obj X) ((D.u d).obj Y₀) (eqToHom hn)
  -- the covering of `Y₀`, transported to the level `m`
  obtain ⟨hd, hdfin⟩ := map_mem_toPrecoverage_and_finite D d hS₀ hS₀fin
  obtain ⟨he, -⟩ := map_mem_toPrecoverage_and_finite D e hd hdfin
  have he' :
    Sieve.generate
        (Presieve.ofArrows (fun r => (D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj (B₀ r)))
          (fun r => (D.u e).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r)))) ∈
      (D.J m) ((D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj Y₀)) := by
    rw [← GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff]
    simpa using he
  -- its pullback along `ξ`, and a finite family generating that pullback
  have hefin :
    Presieve.ofArrows (fun r => (D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj (B₀ r)))
        (fun r => (D.u e).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r))) ∈
      ((D.J m).toPrecoverage ⊓ Precoverage.finite (D.C m))
        ((D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj Y₀)) :=
    ⟨(GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff _ _).2 he',
      Precoverage.ofArrows_mem_finite _ _⟩
  have := D.hasPullbacks m
  have :
    (Presieve.ofArrows (fun r => (D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj (B₀ r)))
        (fun r => (D.u e).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r)))).HasPullbacks ξ :=
    Precoverage.hasPullbacks_of_mem ξ hefin
  obtain ⟨α, hα, B, g, hgen⟩ :=
    StacksWeakAux.exists_finite_generating_pullback
      (fun r => (D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj (B₀ r)))
      (fun r => (D.u e).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r))) ξ
  have hA : (D.u (e ≫ c)).obj X = (D.u e).obj ((D.u c).obj X) := Functor.congr_obj (D.comp e c) X
  have hcov : Presieve.ofArrows B g ∈ (D.J m).toPrecoverage ((D.u e).obj ((D.u c).obj X)) := by
    rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff, hgen]
    exact (D.J m).pullback_stable ξ he'
  refine
    ⟨m, e ≫ c, α, hα, B, fun r => g r ≫ eqToHom hA.symm,
      ofArrows_comp_eqToHom_mem_toPrecoverage (D.J m) hA.symm B g hcov, fun r => ?_⟩
  have hmem :
    (Sieve.generate
          (Presieve.ofArrows (fun r => (D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj (B₀ r)))
            (fun r => (D.u e).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r))))).arrows
      (g r ≫ ξ) := by
    have h0 : (Sieve.generate (Presieve.ofArrows B g)).arrows (g r) :=
      ⟨_, 𝟙 _, g r, Presieve.ofArrows.mk r, by simp⟩
    rw [hgen] at h0
    exact h0
  obtain ⟨W, q, p, hp, hfac⟩ := hmem
  obtain ⟨r₀⟩ := hp
  -- the two object identifications the transports are made of
  have hW : (u m).obj ((D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj (B₀ r₀))) = (u i₀).obj (B₀ r₀) :=
    (Functor.congr_obj (hu e) ((D.u d).obj (B₀ r₀))).trans (Functor.congr_obj (hu d) (B₀ r₀))
  have hWY : (u m).obj ((D.u e).obj ((D.u d).obj Y₀)) = (u i₀).obj Y₀ :=
    (Functor.congr_obj (hu e) ((D.u d).obj Y₀)).trans (Functor.congr_obj (hu d) Y₀)
  -- the image of the member of the covering of `Y₀` lies in `S`
  have hRmem : R ((u i₀).map (g₀ r₀) ≫ eqToHom hY₀) :=
    mem_of_eq_cast hY₀ hReq ((u i₀).map (g₀ r₀)) (Presieve.map_map (Presieve.ofArrows.mk r₀))
  have hRmem' : S.arrows ((u i₀).map (g₀ r₀) ≫ eqToHom hY₀) := by
    apply hRS; exact hRmem
  have hSmem := S.downward_closed hRmem' ((u m).map q ≫ eqToHom hW)
  -- and the member `g r` factors through it, after transport
  have hcomp :
    (u m).map ((D.u e).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r₀))) =
      eqToHom hW ≫ (u i₀).map (g₀ r₀) ≫ eqToHom hWY.symm := by
    have h6 :
      (u m).map ((D.u e).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r₀))) = (D.u e ⋙ u m).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r₀)) :=
      rfl
    have h7 : (u n).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r₀)) = (D.u d ⋙ u n).map (g₀ r₀) := rfl
    rw [h6, Functor.congr_hom (hu e) ((D.u d).map (g₀ r₀)), h7, Functor.congr_hom (hu d) (g₀ r₀)]
    simp
  have h5 :
    ((u m).map (g r) ≫ (u m).map ξ) ≫ eqToHom (hWY.trans hY₀) =
      ((u m).map q ≫ (u m).map ((D.u e).map ((D.u d).map (g₀ r₀)))) ≫ eqToHom (hWY.trans hY₀) := by
    rw [← Functor.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp, hfac]
  rw [hcomp] at h5
  have hgoal :
    (u m).map (g r ≫ eqToHom hA.symm) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu (e ≫ c)) X) =
      ((u m).map q ≫ eqToHom hW) ≫ (u i₀).map (g₀ r₀) ≫ eqToHom hY₀ := by
    simp only [hξ, Functor.map_comp, eqToHom_map, Category.assoc, eqToHom_trans,
      ] at h5 ⊢
    exact h5
  rw [hgoal]
  exact hSmem

/-- **A covering at a level glues sections of the sheaf at that level.** A presieve of `D.C m`
whose generated sieve covers is a sheaf-for presieve for `F m`, so a compatible family of sections
on it has a unique amalgamation. This is the form in which the sheaf property of `F m` is consumed
by the descent, `hS` being what `map_mem_toPrecoverage_and_finite` produces. -/
private lemma isSheafFor_of_mem_toPrecoverage (m : D.I) {Y : D.C m} {S : Presieve Y}
    (hS : S ∈ (D.J m).toPrecoverage Y) : S.IsSheafFor (F m).obj := by
  rw [Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate]
  exact ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).1 (F m).property) _ hS

/-- **Sections of `G` that agree on a covering of `K` are equal.** The separatedness half of the
sheaf property of `G`, for the coverings of Stacks 09YL rather than for a covering sieve; it is
what identifies a section glued at a level with the section of `G` it was built from. -/
private lemma eq_of_map_eq_of_mem {V : C} (R : Presieve V) (hR : R ∈ K V) (s s' : G.obj.obj (op V))
    (h : ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (f : W ⟶ V), R f → G.obj.map f.op s = G.obj.map f.op s') : s = s' := by
  have hGs : Presieve.IsSheaf K.toGrothendieck G.obj :=
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).1 G.property
  have hRs : R.IsSheafFor G.obj :=
    (Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate R).2 (hGs _ (Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hR))
  exact hRs.isSeparatedFor.ext h

include hψ in
/-- **Two sections of one level that agree, member by member, at levels of their own, agree at a
single level.** Let `{g_r : B_r ⟶ X}` be a finite covering in `D.C m` and let `T`, `T'` be sections
of `F m` over `X` whose restrictions along `g_r` become equal at some level below `m`, the level
being allowed to depend on `r`. Then `ψ_c T = ψ_c T'` for a single `c : k ⟶ m`.

The finitely many levels are pushed to a common one by `CategoryTheory.IsCofiltered.wideCospan` —
which is where the finiteness of the coverings of Situation 0A34 is used, and why the arrows must
form a *cone* rather than merely lie below each level: the transported members must be a covering
of one transported base. There the restrictions of `ψ_c T` and `ψ_c T'` along the members agree,
and `F k` is separated for that covering, `D.u c` carrying finite coverings to finite coverings.

This is the last step of the separatedness half of Stacks 09YN, `exists_ψ_eq_of_ι_eq`: it turns
a family of level-wise agreements, one per member of a covering, into the single arrow `b : k ⟶ j`
that the conclusion of Stacks 09YN asks for. -/
private lemma exists_ψ_eq_of_forall_exists {m : D.I} {X : D.C m} (T T' : (F m).obj.obj (op X))
    {α : Type} [Finite α] (B : α → D.C m) (g : ∀ r, B r ⟶ X)
    (hcov : Presieve.ofArrows B g ∈ (D.J m).toPrecoverage X)
    (hfin : Presieve.ofArrows B g ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C m) X)
    (h :
      ∀ r,
        ∃ (l : D.I) (c : l ⟶ m),
          (F l).obj.map ((D.u c).map (g r)).op ((ψ c).app (op X) T) =
            (F l).obj.map ((D.u c).map (g r)).op ((ψ c).app (op X) T')) :
    ∃ (k : D.I) (c : k ⟶ m), (ψ c).app (op X) T = (ψ c).app (op X) T' := by
  classical
  choose lev arr harr using h
  obtain ⟨k, c₀, b, hb⟩ := IsCofiltered.wideCospan arr
  refine ⟨k, c₀, ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨hcov', -⟩ := map_mem_toPrecoverage_and_finite D c₀ hcov hfin
  rw [Presieve.map_ofArrows] at hcov'
  refine (isSheafFor_of_mem_toPrecoverage D F k hcov').isSeparatedFor.ext ?_
  rintro W f ⟨r⟩
  have key := congrArg ((ψ (b r)).app (op ((D.u (arr r)).obj (B r)))) (harr r)
  rw [NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ (b r)) ((D.u (arr r)).map (g r)).op,
    NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ (b r)) ((D.u (arr r)).map (g r)).op] at key
  simp only [Functor.comp_map, Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op] at key
  have hmor :
    eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp (b r) (arr r)) X).symm) ≫
        ((D.u (b r ≫ arr r)).map (g r)).op =
      ((D.u (b r)).map ((D.u (arr r)).map (g r))).op ≫
        eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp (b r) (arr r)) (B r)).symm) := by
    rw [Functor.congr_hom (D.comp (b r) (arr r)) (g r)]
    simp
  rw [← hb r, hψ (arr r) (b r) X T, hψ (arr r) (b r) X T', ← Functor.map_comp_apply, ←
    Functor.map_comp_apply, hmor, Functor.map_comp_apply,
    Functor.map_comp_apply, key]

/-- The morphism `f : W ⟶ u_k(B)` of `C` **factors at the level `n`** through `p : W ⟶ u_n(W')` as
the image of the morphism `f' : W' ⟶ u_e(B)` of `D.C n`. This is the factorisation condition that
appears twice in `Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.AgreeAtLevel`, named so that the moves on
it — precomposing in `C`, pushing the level down, postcomposing with a morphism at the level — are
recorded once. -/
private def FactorsAt {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} {W : C} (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B) {n : D.I} (e : n ⟶ k)
    {W' : D.C n} (p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W') (f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B) : Prop :=
  f = p ≫ (u n).map f' ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu e) B)

/-- Unfolding `FactorsAt`. -/
private lemma factorsAt_iff {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} {W : C} {f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B} {n : D.I}
    {e : n ⟶ k} {W' : D.C n} {p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W'} {f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B} :
    FactorsAt D u hu f e p f' ↔ f = p ≫ (u n).map f' ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu e) B) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- Postcomposing a factorisation with a morphism at the level factors the composite with its
image: this is the restriction move on germs. -/
private lemma FactorsAt.map {k : D.I} {B B₀ : D.C k} {W : C} {f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B₀} {n : D.I}
    {e : n ⟶ k} {W' : D.C n} {p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W'} {f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B₀}
    (hf : FactorsAt D u hu f e p f') (q : B₀ ⟶ B) :
    FactorsAt D u hu (f ≫ (u k).map q) e p (f' ≫ (D.u e).map q) := by
  rw [factorsAt_iff, show f = _ from hf, Functor.map_comp,
    show (u n).map ((D.u e).map q) = (D.u e ⋙ u n).map q from rfl, Functor.congr_hom (hu e) q]
  simp

/-- Pushing a factorisation to a level below: apply `D.u x` to the morphism at the level and
compose the presentation with the identification `u_m ∘ u_x = u_n`. -/
private lemma FactorsAt.push {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} {W : C} {f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B} {n : D.I}
    {e : n ⟶ k} {W' : D.C n} {p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W'} {f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B}
    (hf : FactorsAt D u hu f e p f') {m : D.I} (x : m ⟶ n) :
    FactorsAt D u hu f (x ≫ e) (p ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu x) W').symm)
      ((D.u x).map f' ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x e) B).symm) := by
  rw [factorsAt_iff, show f = _ from hf, Functor.map_comp, eqToHom_map,
    show (u m).map ((D.u x).map f') = (D.u x ⋙ u m).map f' from rfl, Functor.congr_hom (hu x) f']
  simp

/-- `FactorsAt.push` with the composite arrow given a name: the pushed factorisation is at the
level `c` rather than at `x ≫ e`, which is what lets several pushed factorisations be compared. -/
private lemma FactorsAt.pushEq {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} {W : C} {f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B} {n : D.I}
    {e : n ⟶ k} {W' : D.C n} {p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W'} {f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B}
    (hf : FactorsAt D u hu f e p f') {m : D.I} (x : m ⟶ n) (c : m ⟶ k) (hc : x ≫ e = c) :
    FactorsAt D u hu f c (p ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu x) W').symm)
      ((D.u x).map f' ≫
        eqToHom
          ((Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x e) B).symm.trans
            (congrArg (fun z : m ⟶ k => (D.u z).obj B) hc))) := by
  subst hc; exact FactorsAt.push D u hu hf x

/-- **A factorisation of a morphism, composed with a factorisation of its presentation, is a
factorisation at the composite level.** This is the transitivity that makes germs well defined:
the presentation `p : W ⟶ u_n(W')` is itself a morphism of `C` into an object coming from a level,
so it can be factored in turn, and the two factorisations compose. -/
private lemma FactorsAt.trans {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} {W : C} {h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A} {n : D.I}
    {d : n ⟶ j} {W' : D.C n} {p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W'} {h' : W' ⟶ (D.u d).obj A}
    (hh : FactorsAt D u hu h d p h') {m : D.I} {x : m ⟶ n} {W₂ : D.C m} {p₂ : W ⟶ (u m).obj W₂}
    {P : W₂ ⟶ (D.u x).obj W'} (hp : FactorsAt D u hu p x p₂ P) (c : m ⟶ j) (hc : x ≫ d = c) :
    FactorsAt D u hu h c p₂
      (P ≫
        (D.u x).map h' ≫
        eqToHom
          ((Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x d) A).symm.trans
            (congrArg (fun z : m ⟶ j => (D.u z).obj A) hc))) := by
  subst hc
  rw [factorsAt_iff, show h = _ from hh, show p = _ from hp, Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp,
    eqToHom_map, show (u m).map ((D.u x).map h') = (D.u x ⋙ u m).map h' from rfl,
    Functor.congr_hom (hu x) h']
  simp

/-- **Changing the level a factorisation is read at.** A morphism into `u_{k'}(u_a(B))` factors at
the level `e` exactly when the corresponding morphism into `u_k(B)` factors at the level `e ≫ a`.
This is the factorisation half of the invariance of germs under `s ↦ ψ_a s`. -/
private lemma FactorsAt.level_comp_iff {k k' : D.I} (a : k' ⟶ k) {B : D.C k} {W : C}
    (f₀ : W ⟶ (u k').obj ((D.u a).obj B)) {n : D.I} (e : n ⟶ k') {W' : D.C n}
    (p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W') (g : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj ((D.u a).obj B)) :
    FactorsAt D u hu f₀ e p g ↔
      FactorsAt D u hu (f₀ ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) B)) (e ≫ a) p
        (g ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp e a) B).symm) := by
  have hkey :
    (p ≫ (u n).map g ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu e) ((D.u a).obj B))) ≫
        eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) B) =
      p ≫
        (u n).map (g ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp e a) B).symm) ≫
        eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu (e ≫ a)) B) := by
    rw [Functor.map_comp, eqToHom_map]; simp
  constructor
  · intro hf
    rw [factorsAt_iff, ← hkey, ← show f₀ = _ from hf]
  · intro hf
    rw [factorsAt_iff]
    refine (cancel_mono (f := eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) B))).mp ?_
    rw [hkey]
    exact (factorsAt_iff D u hu).1 hf

include hu hobj hhom in
/-- **Two morphisms out of an object of `C` descend to one level, through one presentation.** The
two-morphism form of the descent of finitely many morphisms out of `W` to one level, with the
presentation of `W` displayed as the transport of an identification `u_m(V) = W`; it is the form
every comparison of two germs consumes. -/
private lemma exists_level_presentation₂ (W : C) {k₁ k₂ : D.I} (B₁ : D.C k₁) (B₂ : D.C k₂)
    (f₁ : W ⟶ (u k₁).obj B₁) (f₂ : W ⟶ (u k₂).obj B₂) :
    ∃ (m : D.I) (V : D.C m) (hV : (u m).obj V = W) (e₁ : m ⟶ k₁) (e₂ : m ⟶ k₂) (g₁ :
      V ⟶ (D.u e₁).obj B₁) (g₂ : V ⟶ (D.u e₂).obj B₂),
      FactorsAt D u hu f₁ e₁ (eqToHom hV.symm) g₁ ∧
        FactorsAt D u hu f₂ e₂ (eqToHom hV.symm) g₂ := by
  obtain ⟨l, W₀, rfl⟩ := hobj W
  obtain ⟨m₁, c₁, d₁, gg₁, hgg₁⟩ := exists_level_hom_of_hom D u hu hhom l W₀ k₁ B₁ f₁
  obtain ⟨m₂, c₂, d₂, gg₂, hgg₂⟩ := exists_level_hom_of_hom D u hu hhom l W₀ k₂ B₂ f₂
  obtain ⟨m, x₁, x₂, hx⟩ := IsCofiltered.cospan c₁ c₂
  have E₁ : (D.u (x₁ ≫ c₁)).obj W₀ = (D.u x₁).obj ((D.u c₁).obj W₀) :=
    Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x₁ c₁) W₀
  have E₂ : (D.u (x₁ ≫ c₁)).obj W₀ = (D.u x₂).obj ((D.u c₂).obj W₀) := by
    rw [hx]; exact Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x₂ c₂) W₀
  have T₁ : (D.u x₁).obj ((D.u d₁).obj B₁) = (D.u (x₁ ≫ d₁)).obj B₁ :=
    (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x₁ d₁) B₁).symm
  have T₂ : (D.u x₂).obj ((D.u d₂).obj B₂) = (D.u (x₂ ≫ d₂)).obj B₂ :=
    (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x₂ d₂) B₂).symm
  refine
    ⟨m, (D.u (x₁ ≫ c₁)).obj W₀, Functor.congr_obj (hu (x₁ ≫ c₁)) W₀, x₁ ≫ d₁, x₂ ≫ d₂,
      eqToHom E₁ ≫ (D.u x₁).map gg₁ ≫ eqToHom T₁, eqToHom E₂ ≫ (D.u x₂).map gg₂ ≫ eqToHom T₂, ?_,
      ?_⟩
  · rw [factorsAt_iff, Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp, eqToHom_map, eqToHom_map,
      show (u m).map ((D.u x₁).map gg₁) = (D.u x₁ ⋙ u m).map gg₁ from rfl,
      Functor.congr_hom (hu x₁) gg₁, hgg₁]
    simp
  · rw [factorsAt_iff, Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp, eqToHom_map, eqToHom_map,
      show (u m).map ((D.u x₂).map gg₂) = (D.u x₂ ⋙ u m).map gg₂ from rfl,
      Functor.congr_hom (hu x₂) gg₂, hgg₂]
    simp

include hψ in
/-- **Pushing a restricted section to a level below.** The restriction of `ψ_c s` along the image
of `f'` under `D.u x`, transported along `c = x ≫ e`, is `ψ_x` of the restriction of `ψ_e s` along
`f'`. This is the cocycle identity `hψ` combined with the naturality of `ψ_x`, and it is the
computation every descent in this file performs on the section side. -/
private lemma psi_push_map_eq {k n m : D.I} (e : n ⟶ k) (x : m ⟶ n) (c : m ⟶ k) (hc : x ≫ e = c)
    {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W' : D.C n} (f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B) :
    (F m).obj.map
        ((D.u x).map f' ≫
            eqToHom
              ((Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x e) B).symm.trans
                (congrArg (fun z : m ⟶ k => (D.u z).obj B) hc))).op
        ((ψ c).app (op B) s) =
      (ψ x).app (op W') ((F n).obj.map f'.op ((ψ e).app (op B) s)) := by
  subst hc
  have hmor :
    eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x e) B).symm) ≫
        ((D.u x).map f' ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x e) B).symm).op =
      ((D.u x).map f').op := by
    simp [eqToHom_op]
  rw [hψ e x B s, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, hmor,
    NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ x) f'.op ((ψ e).app (op B) s)]
  simp

include hψ in
/-- **Pushing a factorisation and its germ to a level below.** `FactorsAt.pushEq` together with
`psi_push_map_eq`: the pushed factorisation `M` of `f` at the level `c` computes the germ
`ψ_x` of the one computed by `f'` at the level `e`. -/
private lemma exists_factorsAt_push {k n m : D.I} (e : n ⟶ k) (x : m ⟶ n) (c : m ⟶ k)
    (hc : x ≫ e = c) {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C} {f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B}
    {W' : D.C n} {p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W'} {f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B} (hf : FactorsAt D u hu f e p f') :
    ∃ M : (D.u x).obj W' ⟶ (D.u c).obj B,
      FactorsAt D u hu f c (p ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu x) W').symm) M ∧
        (F m).obj.map M.op ((ψ c).app (op B) s) =
          (ψ x).app (op W') ((F n).obj.map f'.op ((ψ e).app (op B) s)) :=
  ⟨_, FactorsAt.pushEq D u hu hf x c hc, psi_push_map_eq D F ψ hψ e x c hc s f'⟩

include hψ in
/-- The section-side companion of `FactorsAt.trans`: restricting `ψ_c s` along the composite
factorisation is restricting, along the presentation, the `ψ_x` of the restriction of `ψ_e s`. -/
private lemma psi_trans_map_eq {k n m : D.I} (e : n ⟶ k) (x : m ⟶ n) (c : m ⟶ k) (hc : x ≫ e = c)
    {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W' : D.C n} (f' : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B) {W₂ : D.C m}
    (P : W₂ ⟶ (D.u x).obj W') :
    (F m).obj.map
        (P ≫
            (D.u x).map f' ≫
            eqToHom
              ((Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x e) B).symm.trans
                (congrArg (fun z : m ⟶ k => (D.u z).obj B) hc))).op
        ((ψ c).app (op B) s) =
      (F m).obj.map P.op ((ψ x).app (op W') ((F n).obj.map f'.op ((ψ e).app (op B) s))) := by
  rw [← psi_push_map_eq D F ψ hψ e x c hc s f', ← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp]

include hhom_inj in
/-- **Two factorisations of one morphism through one isomorphic presentation and one level agree at
a level below.** The presentation being invertible, the two morphisms of `D.C n` have the same
image in `C`, so `hhom_inj` makes them equal after transport to a lower level. -/
private lemma FactorsAt.exists_hom_eq {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} {W : C} {f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B} {n : D.I}
    {e : n ⟶ k} {W' : D.C n} {p : W ⟶ (u n).obj W'} [IsIso p] {f₁ f₂ : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj B}
    (h₁ : FactorsAt D u hu f e p f₁) (h₂ : FactorsAt D u hu f e p f₂) :
    ∃ (m : D.I) (w : m ⟶ n), (D.u w).map f₁ = (D.u w).map f₂ := by
  refine hhom_inj n W' ((D.u e).obj B) f₁ f₂ ?_
  have hh := (show f = _ from h₁).symm.trans (show f = _ from h₂)
  exact (cancel_mono _).mp ((cancel_epi p).mp hh)

include hψ in
/-- Sections that agree after two successive transitions agree after the composite transition. -/
private lemma psi_comp_inj {i j' k' : D.I} (a : j' ⟶ i) (b : k' ⟶ j') {V : D.C i}
    (X Y : (F i).obj.obj (op V))
    (hXY :
      (ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) X) =
        (ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) Y)) :
    (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) X = (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) Y := by rw [hψ a b V X, hψ a b V Y, hXY]

/-- **Two morphisms at a level with the same image at a lower level restrict a section to the same
germ there.** Naturality of `ψ_w` turns the restriction along `M` followed by the transition into
the transition followed by the restriction along `u_w(M)`, which only depends on `u_w(M)`. -/
private lemma psi_map_congr {n m : D.I} (w : m ⟶ n) {X Y : D.C n} (M₁ M₂ : X ⟶ Y)
    (hM : (D.u w).map M₁ = (D.u w).map M₂) (y : (F n).obj.obj (op Y)) :
    (ψ w).app (op X) ((F n).obj.map M₁.op y) = (ψ w).app (op X) ((F n).obj.map M₂.op y) := by
  rw [NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ w) M₁.op y, NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ w) M₂.op y]
  simp only [Functor.comp_map, Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op]
  rw [hM]

include hu hhom hhom_inj hψ in
/-- **Germs are well defined.** Suppose `s` at the level `k` and `t` at the level `j` agree at a
level along `f` and `h`, and suppose `f` and `h` are *also* factored through one **invertible**
presentation `p₀ : W ≅ u_{m₀}(V)`, as the images of `F₀` and `H₀`. Then the germs those second
factorisations compute — the restrictions of `ψ_{a₁} s` along `F₀` and of `ψ_{a₂} t` along `H₀` —
already agree after a single transition `ψ_x`.

In other words the germ of a section along a morphism of `C` does not depend on the factorisation
chosen to compute it, once one descends far enough. This is the one descent argument of the
separatedness half: the witness's presentation is compared with `p₀` by descending `p₀⁻¹ ≫ p`
(`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.exists_level_hom_of_hom`) — which is where invertibility of
`p₀` is used — the levels of the two factorisations of `f`, and of the two of `h`, are made equal
from below (`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.exists_hom_eq_pair`), and there the
factorisations themselves become equal by `hhom_inj` (`FactorsAt.exists_hom_eq`).
-/
private lemma agree_of_factors {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k : D.I}
    {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C} {f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B} {h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A}
    (hag : AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s f h) {m₀ : D.I} {V : D.C m₀} {p₀ : W ⟶ (u m₀).obj V} [IsIso p₀]
    {a₁ : m₀ ⟶ k} {F₀ : V ⟶ (D.u a₁).obj B} (hf₀ : FactorsAt D u hu f a₁ p₀ F₀) {a₂ : m₀ ⟶ j}
    {H₀ : V ⟶ (D.u a₂).obj A} (hh₀ : FactorsAt D u hu h a₂ p₀ H₀) :
    ∃ (m : D.I) (x : m ⟶ m₀),
      (ψ x).app (op V) ((F m₀).obj.map F₀.op ((ψ a₁).app (op B) s)) =
        (ψ x).app (op V) ((F m₀).obj.map H₀.op ((ψ a₂).app (op A) t)) := by
  obtain ⟨n, e, d, W', p, f', h', hf, hh, heq⟩ := hag
  obtain ⟨m₁, c, dd, σ, hσ0⟩ := exists_level_hom_of_hom D u hu hhom m₀ V n W' (inv p₀ ≫ p)
  have hσ : FactorsAt D u hu p dd (p₀ ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu c) V).symm) σ := by
    rw [factorsAt_iff, hσ0]
    simp
  have hf' : FactorsAt D u hu f e p f' := hf
  have hh' : FactorsAt D u hu h d p h' := hh
  -- the witness's two factorisations, composed with the factorisation of its presentation
  obtain ⟨NfA, hNfA, gNfA⟩ :
    ∃ M : (D.u c).obj V ⟶ (D.u (dd ≫ e)).obj B,
      FactorsAt D u hu f (dd ≫ e) (p₀ ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu c) V).symm) M ∧
        (F m₁).obj.map M.op ((ψ (dd ≫ e)).app (op B) s) =
          (F m₁).obj.map σ.op ((ψ dd).app (op W') ((F n).obj.map f'.op ((ψ e).app (op B) s))) :=
    ⟨_, FactorsAt.trans D u hu hf' hσ (dd ≫ e) rfl,
      psi_trans_map_eq D F ψ hψ e dd (dd ≫ e) rfl s f' σ⟩
  obtain ⟨NhA, hNhA, gNhA⟩ :
    ∃ M : (D.u c).obj V ⟶ (D.u (dd ≫ d)).obj A,
      FactorsAt D u hu h (dd ≫ d) (p₀ ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu c) V).symm) M ∧
        (F m₁).obj.map M.op ((ψ (dd ≫ d)).app (op A) t) =
          (F m₁).obj.map σ.op ((ψ dd).app (op W') ((F n).obj.map h'.op ((ψ d).app (op A) t))) :=
    ⟨_, FactorsAt.trans D u hu hh' hσ (dd ≫ d) rfl,
      psi_trans_map_eq D F ψ hψ d dd (dd ≫ d) rfl t h' σ⟩
  -- the given factorisations, pushed to the level `m₁`
  obtain ⟨MfB, hMfB, gMfB⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ a₁ c (c ≫ a₁) rfl s hf₀
  obtain ⟨MhB, hMhB, gMhB⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ a₂ c (c ≫ a₂) rfl t hh₀
  have hgift :
    (F m₁).obj.map NfA.op ((ψ (dd ≫ e)).app (op B) s) =
      (F m₁).obj.map NhA.op ((ψ (dd ≫ d)).app (op A) t) := by
    rw [gNfA, gNhA, heq]
  -- the four arrows of `D.I` are made equal in pairs from below
  obtain ⟨m₂, z₁, cf, hcf1, hcf2⟩ := exists_hom_eq_pair D (dd ≫ e) (c ≫ a₁)
  obtain ⟨m₃, z₂, cd, hcd1, hcd2⟩ := exists_hom_eq_pair D (z₁ ≫ dd ≫ d) (z₁ ≫ c ≫ a₂)
  have e1 : (z₂ ≫ z₁) ≫ dd ≫ e = z₂ ≫ cf := by rw [Category.assoc, hcf1]
  have e2 : (z₂ ≫ z₁) ≫ c ≫ a₁ = z₂ ≫ cf := by rw [Category.assoc, hcf2]
  have e3 : (z₂ ≫ z₁) ≫ dd ≫ d = cd := by
    rw [Category.assoc]; exact hcd1
  have e4 : (z₂ ≫ z₁) ≫ c ≫ a₂ = cd := by
    rw [Category.assoc]; exact hcd2
  -- all four factorisations, pushed to the level `m₃` where the arrows agree
  obtain ⟨NfA1, hNfA1, gNfA1⟩ :=
    exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ (dd ≫ e) (z₂ ≫ z₁) (z₂ ≫ cf) e1 s hNfA
  obtain ⟨MfB1, hMfB1, gMfB1⟩ :=
    exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ (c ≫ a₁) (z₂ ≫ z₁) (z₂ ≫ cf) e2 s hMfB
  obtain ⟨NhA1, hNhA1, gNhA1⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ (dd ≫ d) (z₂ ≫ z₁) cd e3 t hNhA
  obtain ⟨MhB1, hMhB1, gMhB1⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ (c ≫ a₂) (z₂ ≫ z₁) cd e4 t hMhB
  have hgift1 :
    (F m₃).obj.map NfA1.op ((ψ (z₂ ≫ cf)).app (op B) s) =
      (F m₃).obj.map NhA1.op ((ψ cd).app (op A) t) := by
    rw [gNfA1, gNhA1, hgift]
  -- the two factorisations of `f` become equal at a level, so the two germs agree there
  obtain ⟨m₄, w₁, hw₁⟩ := FactorsAt.exists_hom_eq D u hu hhom_inj hNfA1 hMfB1
  have hstep6 :
    (ψ w₁).app (op ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V)))
        ((F m₃).obj.map MfB1.op ((ψ (z₂ ≫ cf)).app (op B) s)) =
      (ψ w₁).app (op ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V)))
        ((F m₃).obj.map NhA1.op ((ψ cd).app (op A) t)) := by
    rw [← hgift1, ← psi_map_congr D F ψ w₁ NfA1 MfB1 hw₁ ((ψ (z₂ ≫ cf)).app (op B) s)]
  -- the two factorisations of `h`, pushed to that level
  obtain ⟨NhA2, hNhA2, gNhA2⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ cd w₁ (w₁ ≫ cd) rfl t hNhA1
  obtain ⟨MhB2, hMhB2, gMhB2⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ cd w₁ (w₁ ≫ cd) rfl t hMhB1
  -- and the two factorisations of `h` become equal one level further down
  obtain ⟨m₅, w₂, hw₂⟩ := FactorsAt.exists_hom_eq D u hu hhom_inj hNhA2 hMhB2
  have hstep7 :
    (ψ w₂).app (op ((D.u w₁).obj ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V))))
        ((ψ w₁).app (op ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V)))
          ((F m₃).obj.map NhA1.op ((ψ cd).app (op A) t))) =
      (ψ w₂).app (op ((D.u w₁).obj ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V))))
        ((ψ w₁).app (op ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V)))
          ((F m₃).obj.map MhB1.op ((ψ cd).app (op A) t))) := by
    rw [← gNhA2, ← gMhB2]
    exact psi_map_congr D F ψ w₂ NhA2 MhB2 hw₂ ((ψ (w₁ ≫ cd)).app (op A) t)
  -- unwinding the germ identities: the two sides of the goal, after four transitions
  have hfinal :
    (ψ w₂).app (op ((D.u w₁).obj ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V))))
        ((ψ w₁).app (op ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V)))
          ((ψ (z₂ ≫ z₁)).app (op ((D.u c).obj V))
            ((ψ c).app (op V) ((F m₀).obj.map F₀.op ((ψ a₁).app (op B) s))))) =
      (ψ w₂).app (op ((D.u w₁).obj ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V))))
        ((ψ w₁).app (op ((D.u (z₂ ≫ z₁)).obj ((D.u c).obj V)))
          ((ψ (z₂ ≫ z₁)).app (op ((D.u c).obj V))
            ((ψ c).app (op V) ((F m₀).obj.map H₀.op ((ψ a₂).app (op A) t))))) := by
    rw [← gMfB, ← gMhB, ← gMfB1, ← gMhB1, hstep6, hstep7]
  refine ⟨m₅, ((w₂ ≫ w₁) ≫ (z₂ ≫ z₁)) ≫ c, ?_⟩
  refine psi_comp_inj D F ψ hψ c ((w₂ ≫ w₁) ≫ (z₂ ≫ z₁)) _ _ ?_
  refine psi_comp_inj D F ψ hψ (z₂ ≫ z₁) (w₂ ≫ w₁) _ _ ?_
  exact psi_comp_inj D F ψ hψ w₁ w₂ _ _ hfinal

/-- **Restricting a section before or after a transition.** The transition `ψ_e` of the restriction
of `s` along `q` is the restriction of `ψ_e s` along the image of `q`: the naturality of `ψ e`. -/
private lemma psi_map_op_eq {k n : D.I} (e : n ⟶ k) {B B₀ : D.C k} (q : B₀ ⟶ B)
    (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) :
    (ψ e).app (op B₀) ((F k).obj.map q.op s) =
      (F n).obj.map ((D.u e).map q).op ((ψ e).app (op B) s) := by
  simpa only [Functor.comp_map, Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op] using
    NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ e) q.op s

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hψ in
/-- **Agreement at a level is invariant under restriction at the level.** Restricting `s` along a
morphism `q` of `D.C k` and restricting the morphism `f` of `C` along the image of `q` describe the
same germ, so they cut out the same sieve of agreement with `t`.

The inclusion from left to right is formal — postcompose the factorisation of `f` with `u_e(q)`.
The converse is the descent: a factorisation of `f ≫ u_k(q)` says nothing about `f` until `f` and
the presentation the factorisation uses are brought to one level
(`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.exists_level_presentation₂`), where the two resulting
factorisations of one morphism of `C` become equal at a further level by `hhom_inj`. -/
private lemma agreeSieve_map {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k : D.I}
    {B B₀ : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) (q : B₀ ⟶ B) {W : C} (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B₀)
    (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A) :
    agreeSieve hu ψ t ((F k).obj.map q.op s) f h = agreeSieve hu ψ t s (f ≫ (u k).map q) h := by
  suffices H :
    ∀ {W : C} (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B₀) (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A),
      AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t ((F k).obj.map q.op s) f h ↔ AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s (f ≫ (u k).map q) h
    by
    ext W₀ c
    rw [agreeSieve_apply, agreeSieve_apply]
    rw [← Category.assoc]
    exact H (c ≫ f) (c ≫ h)
  clear f h
  intro W f h
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨n, e, d, W', p, f', h', hf, hh, heq⟩
    refine ⟨n, e, d, W', p, f' ≫ (D.u e).map q, h', FactorsAt.map D u hu hf q, hh, ?_⟩
    rw [op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply, ← psi_map_op_eq D F ψ e q s]
    exact heq
  · intro hag
    obtain ⟨m₀, V, hV, a₁, a₂, F₀, H₀, hf₀, hh₀⟩ :=
      exists_level_presentation₂ D u hu hobj hhom W B₀ A f h
    obtain ⟨m, x, hx⟩ :=
      agree_of_factors D u hu hhom hhom_inj F ψ hψ t s hag (FactorsAt.map D u hu hf₀ q) hh₀
    obtain ⟨Xf, hXf, hpushf⟩ :=
      exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ a₁ x (x ≫ a₁) rfl ((F k).obj.map q.op s) hf₀
    obtain ⟨Xh, hXh, hpushh⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ a₂ x (x ≫ a₂) rfl t hh₀
    refine
      ⟨m, x ≫ a₁, x ≫ a₂, (D.u x).obj V,
        eqToHom hV.symm ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu x) V).symm, Xf, Xh, hXf, hXh, ?_⟩
    rw [hpushf, hpushh, psi_map_op_eq D F ψ a₁ q s, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp]
    exact hx

include hψ in
/-- **Changing the level a restricted section is read at.** The level-change companion of
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.psi_push_map_eq`: restricting `ψ_{e ≫ a} s` along the
transport of `gg` is restricting `ψ_e (ψ_a s)` along `gg`. -/
private lemma psi_level_comp_eq {k k' n : D.I} (a : k' ⟶ k) (e : n ⟶ k') {B : D.C k}
    (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W' : D.C n} (gg : W' ⟶ (D.u e).obj ((D.u a).obj B)) :
    (F n).obj.map (gg ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp e a) B).symm).op
        ((ψ (e ≫ a)).app (op B) s) =
      (F n).obj.map gg.op ((ψ e).app (op ((D.u a).obj B)) ((ψ a).app (op B) s)) := by
  have hmor :
    eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp e a) B).symm) ≫
        (gg ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp e a) B).symm).op =
      gg.op := by
    simp [eqToHom_op]
  rw [hψ a e B s, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, hmor]

include hu hψ in
/-- **Agreement at a level is invariant under passage to a lower level.** The germ of `ψ_a s` along
`f₀` is the germ of `s` along the corresponding morphism into `u_k(B)`, so the two cut out the same
sieve of agreement with `t`. Both directions only move the level of the witness along a cospan of
`D.I` (`CategoryTheory.IsCofiltered.cospan`); no presentation of `W` is needed. -/
private lemma agreeSieve_psi {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k k' : D.I}
    (a : k' ⟶ k) {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C}
    (f₀ : W ⟶ (u k').obj ((D.u a).obj B)) (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A) :
    agreeSieve hu ψ t ((ψ a).app (op B) s) f₀ h =
      agreeSieve hu ψ t s (f₀ ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) B)) h := by
  suffices H :
    ∀ {W : C} (f₀ : W ⟶ (u k').obj ((D.u a).obj B)) (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A),
      AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t ((ψ a).app (op B) s) f₀ h ↔
        AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s (f₀ ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) B)) h
    by
    ext W₀ c
    rw [agreeSieve_apply, agreeSieve_apply]
    rw [← Category.assoc]
    exact H (c ≫ f₀) (c ≫ h)
  clear f₀ h
  intro W f₀ h
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨n, e, d, W', p, f', h', hf, hh, heq⟩
    exact
      ⟨n, e ≫ a, d, W', p, _, h', (FactorsAt.level_comp_iff D u hu a f₀ e p f').1 hf, hh, by
        rw [psi_level_comp_eq D F ψ hψ a e s f']; exact heq⟩
  · rintro ⟨n, e, d, W', p, f', h', hf, hh, heq⟩
    obtain ⟨n', x, y, hxy⟩ := IsCofiltered.cospan e a
    obtain ⟨Xf, hXf, hpushf⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ e x (y ≫ a) hxy s hf
    obtain ⟨Xh, hXh, hpushh⟩ := exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ d x (x ≫ d) rfl t hh
    have hc :
      (Xf ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp y a) B)) ≫
          eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp y a) B).symm =
        Xf := by
      simp
    refine
      ⟨n', y, x ≫ d, (D.u x).obj W', p ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu x) W').symm,
        Xf ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp y a) B), Xh, ?_, hXh, ?_⟩
    · refine (FactorsAt.level_comp_iff D u hu a f₀ y _ _).2 ?_
      rw [hc]
      exact hXf
    · rw [← psi_level_comp_eq D F ψ hψ a y s (Xf ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp y a) B)), hc,
        hpushf, hpushh, heq]

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK hψ in
/-- **Agreement at a level is local on `C`.** If the sieve of agreement of `s` and `t` covers, then
`s` and `t` already agree at a level.

The covering sieve is refined by a finite covering at a level
(`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.exists_level_covering`), `f` and `h` are brought to that
level as well, the finitely many levels the members' witnesses live at are pushed to a common one
(`CategoryTheory.IsCofiltered.wideCospan`), and there the two germs agree on a covering, hence
agree, `F` at that level being separated. -/
private lemma agreeAtLevel_of_mem_toGrothendieck {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A))
    {k : D.I} {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C} (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B)
    (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A) (hcov : agreeSieve hu ψ t s f h ∈ K.toGrothendieck W) :
    AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s f h := by
  obtain ⟨m₀, V, hV, a₁, a₂, F₀, H₀, hf₀, hh₀⟩ :=
    exists_level_presentation₂ D u hu hobj hhom W B A f h
  subst hV
  obtain ⟨m, a, β, hβ, Bs, gs, hcovm, hmem⟩ :=
    exists_level_covering D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK m₀ V (agreeSieve hu ψ t s f h) hcov
  have := hβ
  -- the members of the covering, read as elements of the sieve of agreement
  have hag :
    ∀ r : β,
      AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t s (((u m).map (gs r) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)) ≫ f)
        (((u m).map (gs r) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)) ≫ h) :=
    hmem
  -- the canonical factorisations of `f` and `h`, pushed to the level `m`
  obtain ⟨Ff, hf₁⟩ :
    ∃ Ff : (D.u a).obj V ⟶ (D.u (a ≫ a₁)).obj B,
      FactorsAt D u hu f (a ≫ a₁)
        (eqToHom (rfl : (u m₀).obj V = (u m₀).obj V) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)
        Ff :=
    ⟨_, FactorsAt.pushEq D u hu hf₀ a (a ≫ a₁) rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨Fh, hh₁⟩ :
    ∃ Fh : (D.u a).obj V ⟶ (D.u (a ≫ a₂)).obj A,
      FactorsAt D u hu h (a ≫ a₂)
        (eqToHom (rfl : (u m₀).obj V = (u m₀).obj V) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)
        Fh :=
    ⟨_, FactorsAt.pushEq D u hu hh₀ a (a ≫ a₂) rfl⟩
  -- the canonical factorisations of the restrictions to the members, through the identity
  have hfr :
    ∀ r : β,
      FactorsAt D u hu (((u m).map (gs r) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)) ≫ f) (a ≫ a₁)
        (𝟙 ((u m).obj (Bs r))) (gs r ≫ Ff) := by
    intro r
    rw [factorsAt_iff, show f = _ from hf₁]
    simp
  have hhr :
    ∀ r : β,
      FactorsAt D u hu (((u m).map (gs r) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)) ≫ h) (a ≫ a₂)
        (𝟙 ((u m).obj (Bs r))) (gs r ≫ Fh) := by
    intro r
    rw [factorsAt_iff, show h = _ from hh₁]
    simp
  -- the two germs at the level `m`
  obtain ⟨T, hT⟩ :
    ∃ T : (F m).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj V)),
      T = (F m).obj.map Ff.op ((ψ (a ≫ a₁)).app (op B) s) :=
    ⟨_, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨T', hT'⟩ :
    ∃ T' : (F m).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj V)),
      T' = (F m).obj.map Fh.op ((ψ (a ≫ a₂)).app (op A) t) :=
    ⟨_, rfl⟩
  -- they agree on each member of the covering, at a level depending on the member
  have key :
    ∀ r : β,
      ∃ (l : D.I) (c : l ⟶ m),
        (F l).obj.map ((D.u c).map (gs r)).op ((ψ c).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) T) =
          (F l).obj.map ((D.u c).map (gs r)).op ((ψ c).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) T') := by
    intro r
    obtain ⟨mr, xr, hxr⟩ :=
      agree_of_factors D u hu hhom hhom_inj F ψ hψ t s (hag r) (hfr r) (hhr r)
    refine ⟨mr, xr, ?_⟩
    have n1 := NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ xr) (gs r).op T
    have n2 := NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ xr) (gs r).op T'
    simp only [Functor.comp_map, Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op] at n1 n2
    rw [← n1, ← n2, hT, hT', ← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, ←
      op_comp, ← op_comp]
    exact hxr
  -- hence at a single level, `F m` being separated for the covering
  obtain ⟨kk, c, hc⟩ :=
    exists_ψ_eq_of_forall_exists D F ψ hψ T T' Bs gs hcovm (Precoverage.ofArrows_mem_finite Bs gs)
      key
  -- and the witness of agreement at that level
  obtain ⟨Ff', hf₂, hFf'⟩ :=
    exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ (a ≫ a₁) c (c ≫ (a ≫ a₁)) rfl s hf₁
  obtain ⟨Fh', hh₂, hFh'⟩ :=
    exists_factorsAt_push D u hu F ψ hψ (a ≫ a₂) c (c ≫ (a ≫ a₂)) rfl t hh₁
  refine ⟨kk, c ≫ (a ≫ a₁), c ≫ (a ≫ a₂), (D.u c).obj ((D.u a).obj V), _, Ff', Fh', hf₂, hh₂, ?_⟩
  rw [hFf', hFh', ← hT, ← hT']
  exact hc

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK hψ in
/-- The sieve of agreement at a level is `K`-closed: this is
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.agreeAtLevel_of_mem_toGrothendieck` at each morphism of the
sieve, the pullback of the sieve being again a sieve of agreement
(`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.agreeSieve_pullback`). -/
private lemma agreeSieve_isClosed {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k : D.I}
    {B : D.C k} (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) {W : C} (f : W ⟶ (u k).obj B) (h : W ⟶ (u j).obj A) :
    K.toGrothendieck.IsClosed (agreeSieve hu ψ t s f h) := by
  intro W₀ c hc
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff, agreeSieve_pullback] at hc
  exact agreeAtLevel_of_mem_toGrothendieck D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ t s _ _ hc

include hu hhom hhom_inj hψ in
/-- **Two sections of one level whose germs agree along the identity agree at a level.** This is
the extraction step of the separatedness argument: the witness of agreement along the identity of
`u_j(A)` exhibits `A` as a retract, at a level, of the object the witness lives over, and
restricting the equality of germs along that retraction is the conclusion.

The presentation the witness uses is descended by
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.exists_level_presentation₂`; the finitely many arrows of
`D.I` involved are made equal from below by
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.exists_hom_eq_pair`, and that the retraction is the
identity at a level is `hhom_inj`. -/
private lemma exists_ψ_eq_of_agreeAtLevel_id {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} (t t' : (F j).obj.obj (op A))
    (hag : AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t t' (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) (𝟙 ((u j).obj A))) :
    ∃ (k : D.I) (b : k ⟶ j), (ψ b).app (op A) t = (ψ b).app (op A) t' := by
  have hF₀ :
    FactorsAt D u hu (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) (𝟙 j) (𝟙 ((u j).obj A))
      (eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.id_map j) A).symm) := by
    simp [factorsAt_iff, eqToHom_map]
  obtain ⟨m, x, hx⟩ := agree_of_factors D u hu hhom hhom_inj F ψ hψ t t' hag hF₀ hF₀
  have hE : op ((D.u (x ≫ 𝟙 j)).obj A) = op ((D.u x).obj A) := by rw [Category.comp_id]
  have hmor :
    ((D.u x).map (eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.id_map j) A).symm) ≫
          eqToHom
            ((Functor.congr_obj (D.comp x (𝟙 j)) A).symm.trans
              (congrArg (fun z : m ⟶ j => (D.u z).obj A) (rfl : x ≫ 𝟙 j = x ≫ 𝟙 j)))).op =
      eqToHom hE := by
    simp [eqToHom_map, eqToHom_op]
  have hkey :
    ∀ w : (F j).obj.obj (op A),
      (ψ x).app (op A)
          ((F j).obj.map (eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.id_map j) A).symm).op
            ((ψ (𝟙 j)).app (op A) w)) =
        (F m).obj.map (eqToHom hE) ((ψ (x ≫ 𝟙 j)).app (op A) w) := by
    intro w
    rw [←
      psi_push_map_eq D F ψ hψ (𝟙 j) x (x ≫ 𝟙 j) rfl w (W' := A) (f' :=
        eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (D.id_map j) A).symm),
      hmor]
  rw [hkey t', hkey t] at hx
  exact ⟨m, x ≫ 𝟙 j, (map_eqToHom_injective (F m).obj hE hx).symm⟩

/-- **The section of the sheaf `Ω^{yZ}` of `K`-closed relations to `Z = u_j(A)` attached to a
section `s` of `F k` over `B`.** It sends a pair of a morphism `a : W ⟶ u_k(B)` — the structure
morphism of an object of `Over u_k(B)` — and a morphism `b : W ⟶ Z` to the sieve of the morphisms
along which `s` and `t` agree at a level, which is `K`-closed by
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.agreeSieve_isClosed`. Naturality in `Over u_k(B)` is
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.agreeSieve_pullback`. -/
private def relSection {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) {k : D.I} {B : D.C k}
    (s : (F k).obj.obj (op B)) : (relSheaf K ((u j).obj A)).obj.obj (op ((u k).obj B))
    where
  app V :=
    ↾fun b =>
      ⟨agreeSieve hu ψ t s V.unop.hom b,
        agreeSieve_isClosed D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ t s V.unop.hom b⟩
  naturality := by
    rintro ⟨V₁⟩ ⟨V₂⟩ ⟨ρ⟩
    apply ConcreteCategory.hom_ext
    intro b
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    change agreeSieve hu ψ t s V₂.hom (ρ.left ≫ b) = (agreeSieve hu ψ t s V₁.hom b).pullback ρ.left
    rw [agreeSieve_pullback, Over.w ρ]

/-- **The map `F i ⟶ u_i^p Ω^{yZ}` recording agreement at a level with `t`.** Its naturality is the
invariance of germs under restriction at the level,
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections.agreeSieve_map`. -/
private def relMap {j : D.I} {A : D.C j} (t : (F j).obj.obj (op A)) (i : D.I) :
    (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ (relSheaf K ((u j).obj A)).obj
    where
  app _ := ↾fun s => relSection D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ t s
  naturality := by
    rintro ⟨B₁⟩ ⟨B₂⟩ ⟨q⟩
    apply ConcreteCategory.hom_ext
    intro s
    apply NatTrans.ext
    funext V
    apply ConcreteCategory.hom_ext
    intro b
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    exact agreeSieve_map D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj F ψ hψ t s q V.unop.hom b

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK hψ hι hG in
omit hι in
/-- **Separatedness of the colimit description.** Two sections of `F j` over an object `A` of
`D.C j` with the same image under `ι j` agree after applying `ψ b` for some `b : k ⟶ j`.

Two such sections have the same image in `G`, hence agree locally on `u_j(A)`; a covering
witnessing this comes from a finite covering at a level below `j`, and pushing the finitely many
indices to a common level makes the two sections agree there, by separatedness of the sheaf at that
level.

Stated for an arbitrary object `A` of `D.C j`, not only for one of the form `u_a(X)` as the
conclusion of Stacks 09YN is: the gluing lemma `comesFromLevel_amalgamate` consumes it at the fibre
products of the members of a covering, which are not of that form, and the proof never uses that
`A` is transported from a level above. -/
private lemma exists_ψ_eq_of_ι_eq (j : D.I) (A : D.C j) (t t' : (F j).obj.obj (op A))
    (h : (ι j).app (op A) t = (ι j).app (op A) t') :
    ∃ (k : D.I) (b : k ⟶ j), (ψ b).app (op A) t = (ψ b).app (op A) t' := by
  -- the family `relMap` is compatible with the `ψ a`, by invariance of germs under level change
  have hcompat :
    ∀ {i i' : D.I} (a : i' ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
      (relMap D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ t i).app (op V) x =
        (relSheaf K ((u j).obj A)).obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
          ((relMap D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ t i').app (op ((D.u a).obj V))
            ((ψ a).app (op V) x)) := by
    intro i i' a V x
    apply NatTrans.ext
    funext P
    apply ConcreteCategory.hom_ext
    intro b
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    change
      agreeSieve hu ψ t x (unop P).hom b =
        agreeSieve hu ψ t ((ψ a).app (op V) x)
          ((unop P).hom ≫ (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V))).unop) b
    rw [agreeSieve_psi D u hu F ψ hψ t a x _ b]
    congr 1
    simp
  obtain ⟨hmap, hmapspec, -⟩ :=
    hG (relSheaf K ((u j).obj A)) (relMap D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ t) hcompat
  -- the two sections of `Ω^{y u_j(A)}` attached to `t` and to `t'` agree, since `ι j t = ι j t'`
  have key :
    relSection D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ t t =
      relSection D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ t t' := by
    have h1 := hmapspec j A t
    have h2 := hmapspec j A t'
    rw [h] at h1
    exact h1.trans h2.symm
  -- reading that agreement at the identity of `u_j(A)`
  have key2 :
    agreeSieve hu ψ t t (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) =
      agreeSieve hu ψ t t' (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) :=
    congrArg Subtype.val
      (congrArg
        (fun σ : (relSheaf K ((u j).obj A)).obj.obj (op ((u j).obj A)) =>
          σ.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)))) (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)))
        key)
  have hmem :
    (agreeSieve hu ψ t t (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) (𝟙 ((u j).obj A))).arrows (𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) := by
    simpa [agreeSieve_apply] using agreeAtLevel_self hu ψ t
  rw [key2] at hmem
  have hmem' :
    AgreeAtLevel hu ψ t t' (𝟙 ((u j).obj A) ≫ 𝟙 ((u j).obj A))
      (𝟙 ((u j).obj A) ≫ 𝟙 ((u j).obj A)) :=
    hmem
  simp only [Category.id_comp] at hmem'
  exact exists_ψ_eq_of_agreeAtLevel_id D u hu hhom hhom_inj F ψ hψ t t' hmem'

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK hψ hι hG in
/-- **Gluing of sections that come from a level.** A section of `G` over `Z` glued from a
compatible family, indexed by a covering `R` of `K`, of sections that come from a level itself
comes from a level.

The covering `R` is the image of a finite covering at some level; since it is finite and `D.I` is
cofiltered, the finitely many levels of the members of the family can be pushed to a single level
below it, where the family becomes a compatible family of sections of `F` at that level, and the
sheaf property of that `F` glues them. -/
private lemma comesFromLevel_amalgamate (Z : C) (R : Presieve Z) (hR : R ∈ K Z)
    (y : Presieve.FamilyOfElements G.obj R) (hy : y.Compatible)
    (hlev : ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (r : W ⟶ Z) (hr : R r), ComesFromLevel ι W (y r hr)) (t : G.obj.obj (op Z))
    (ht : y.IsAmalgamation t) : ComesFromLevel ι Z t := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨i₀, Y₀, hZ, α, hα, B, g, hcov, hReq⟩ := exists_finite_arrows_of_mem D u K hK Z R hR
  have := hα
  have hfin : Presieve.ofArrows B g ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i₀) Y₀ :=
    Precoverage.ofArrows_mem_finite B g
  obtain ⟨mr, hmrdef⟩ :
    ∃ mr : ∀ r : α, (u i₀).obj (B r) ⟶ Z, ∀ r, mr r = (u i₀).map (g r) ≫ eqToHom hZ :=
    ⟨_, fun _ => rfl⟩
  have hmr : ∀ r, R (mr r) := by
    intro r
    rw [hmrdef]
    exact mem_of_eq_cast hZ hReq ((u i₀).map (g r)) (Presieve.map_map (Presieve.ofArrows.mk r))
  have hstep :
    ∀ r : α,
      ∃ (n : D.I) (e : n ⟶ i₀) (s : (F n).obj.obj (op ((D.u e).obj (B r)))),
        G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu e) (B r))))
            ((ι n).app (op ((D.u e).obj (B r))) s) =
          y (mr r) (hmr r) :=
    fun r =>
    exists_level_of_comesFromLevel D u hu hhom K F ψ G ι hι i₀ (B r) _ (hlev (mr r) (hmr r))
  choose l e s hs using hstep
  obtain ⟨m, a₀, b, hb⟩ := IsCofiltered.wideCospan e
  have eqr : ∀ r, (D.u (b r)).obj ((D.u (e r)).obj (B r)) = (D.u a₀).obj (B r) := by
    intro r
    rw [← hb r]
    exact (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp (b r) (e r)) (B r)).symm
  obtain ⟨S, hSdef⟩ :
    ∃ S : ∀ r, (F m).obj.obj (op ((D.u a₀).obj (B r))),
      ∀ r,
        S r =
          (F m).obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (eqr r)))
            ((ψ (b r)).app (op ((D.u (e r)).obj (B r))) (s r)) :=
    ⟨_, fun _ => rfl⟩
  have hSι :
    ∀ r,
      G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r))))
          ((ι m).app (op ((D.u a₀).obj (B r))) (S r)) =
        y (mr r) (hmr r) := by
    intro r
    have key :
      (u m).op.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (eqr r))) ≫
          eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r))) =
        eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu (b r)) ((D.u (e r)).obj (B r)))) ≫
          eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu (e r)) (B r))) := by
      simp [eqToHom_map]
    rw [hSdef r, NatTrans.naturality_apply (ι m) (eqToHom (congrArg op (eqr r))), ← hs r,
      hι (b r) ((D.u (e r)).obj (B r)) (s r)]
    simp only [Functor.comp_map]
    rw [← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, key]
  -- the level-`m` covering of `(D.u a₀).obj Y₀`
  obtain ⟨π, hπ⟩ :
    ∃ π : ∀ r : α, (D.u a₀).obj (B r) ⟶ (D.u a₀).obj Y₀, π = fun r => (D.u a₀).map (g r) :=
    ⟨_, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨hcovm, hfinm⟩ := map_mem_toPrecoverage_and_finite D a₀ hcov hfin
  rw [Presieve.map_ofArrows, ← hπ] at hcovm hfinm
  have k :
    ∀ r,
      eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r)) ≫ mr r =
        (u m).map (π r) ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) Y₀) ≫ eqToHom hZ := by
    intro r
    have h6 : (u m).map (π r) = (D.u a₀ ⋙ u m).map (g r) := by
      rw [hπ]; rfl
    rw [hmrdef, h6, Functor.congr_hom (hu a₀) (g r)]
    simp
  have := D.hasPullbacks m
  have hpp : (Presieve.ofArrows (fun r => (D.u a₀).obj (B r)) π).HasPairwisePullbacks :=
    Precoverage.hasPairwisePullbacks_of_mem ((D.J m).toPrecoverage ⊓ Precoverage.finite (D.C m))
      ⟨hcovm, hfinm⟩
  have hpair :
    ∀ p : α × α,
      ∃ (kk : D.I) (c : kk ⟶ m),
        (ψ c).app (op (Limits.pullback (π p.1) (π p.2)))
            ((F m).obj.map (Limits.pullback.fst (π p.1) (π p.2)).op (S p.1)) =
          (ψ c).app (op (Limits.pullback (π p.1) (π p.2)))
            ((F m).obj.map (Limits.pullback.snd (π p.1) (π p.2)).op (S p.2)) := by
    rintro ⟨r₁, r₂⟩
    refine exists_ψ_eq_of_ι_eq D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ G ι hG m _ _ _ ?_
    have hcomm :
      ((u m).map (Limits.pullback.fst (π r₁) (π r₂)) ≫
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r₁))) ≫
          mr r₁ =
        ((u m).map (Limits.pullback.snd (π r₁) (π r₂)) ≫
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r₂))) ≫
          mr r₂ := by
      rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, k, k, ← Functor.map_comp_assoc, ← Functor.map_comp_assoc,
        Limits.pullback.condition]
    have h :=
      hy
        ((u m).map (Limits.pullback.fst (π r₁) (π r₂)) ≫
          eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r₁)))
        ((u m).map (Limits.pullback.snd (π r₁) (π r₂)) ≫
          eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r₂)))
        (hmr r₁) (hmr r₂) hcomm
    rw [← hSι r₁, ← hSι r₂] at h
    rw [NatTrans.naturality_apply (ι m) (Limits.pullback.fst (π r₁) (π r₂)).op,
      NatTrans.naturality_apply (ι m) (Limits.pullback.snd (π r₁) (π r₂)).op]
    simp only [Functor.comp_map, Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op]
    simp only [op_comp, eqToHom_op, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, eqToHom_trans_assoc,
      eqToHom_refl, Category.id_comp] at h
    exact h
  -- the further level `m'` at which the family becomes compatible
  choose kk cc hcc using hpair
  obtain ⟨m', c₀, b', hb'⟩ := IsCofiltered.wideCospan cc
  have hcc' :
    ∀ p : α × α,
      (ψ c₀).app (op (Limits.pullback (π p.1) (π p.2)))
          ((F m).obj.map (Limits.pullback.fst (π p.1) (π p.2)).op (S p.1)) =
        (ψ c₀).app (op (Limits.pullback (π p.1) (π p.2)))
          ((F m).obj.map (Limits.pullback.snd (π p.1) (π p.2)).op (S p.2)) := by
    intro p
    rw [← hb' p, hψ (cc p) (b' p), hψ (cc p) (b' p), hcc p]
  obtain ⟨S', hS'def⟩ :
    ∃ S' : ∀ r, (F m').obj.obj (op ((D.u c₀).obj ((D.u a₀).obj (B r)))),
      ∀ r, S' r = (ψ c₀).app (op ((D.u a₀).obj (B r))) (S r) :=
    ⟨_, fun _ => rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨hcovm', hfinm'⟩ := map_mem_toPrecoverage_and_finite D c₀ hcovm hfinm
  rw [Presieve.map_ofArrows] at hcovm' hfinm'
  have hcompat : Presieve.Arrows.Compatible (F m').obj (fun r => (D.u c₀).map (π r)) S' := by
    rintro r₁ r₂ TT q₁ q₂ hq
    have : Limits.PreservesLimit (Limits.cospan (π r₁) (π r₂)) (D.u c₀) :=
      D.preservesPullbacks c₀ (R := Presieve.ofArrows (fun r => (D.u a₀).obj (B r)) π)
        ⟨hcovm, hfinm⟩ (Presieve.ofArrows.mk r₂) (π r₁)
    have : Limits.HasPullback ((D.u c₀).map (π r₁)) ((D.u c₀).map (π r₂)) :=
      Limits.hasPullback_of_preservesPullback (D.u c₀) (π r₁) (π r₂)
    obtain ⟨Q, hQ⟩ :
      ∃ Q : TT ⟶ (D.u c₀).obj (Limits.pullback (π r₁) (π r₂)),
        Q =
          Limits.pullback.lift q₁ q₂ hq ≫
            (Limits.PreservesPullback.iso (D.u c₀) (π r₁) (π r₂)).inv :=
      ⟨_, rfl⟩
    have hq1 : Q ≫ (D.u c₀).map (Limits.pullback.fst (π r₁) (π r₂)) = q₁ := by
      rw [hQ]; simp [Limits.pullback.lift_fst]
    have hq2 : Q ≫ (D.u c₀).map (Limits.pullback.snd (π r₁) (π r₂)) = q₂ := by
      rw [hQ]; simp [Limits.pullback.lift_snd]
    have inner :
      (F m').obj.map ((D.u c₀).map (Limits.pullback.fst (π r₁) (π r₂))).op (S' r₁) =
        (F m').obj.map ((D.u c₀).map (Limits.pullback.snd (π r₁) (π r₂))).op (S' r₂) := by
      have n1 := NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ c₀) (Limits.pullback.fst (π r₁) (π r₂)).op (S r₁)
      have n2 := NatTrans.naturality_apply (ψ c₀) (Limits.pullback.snd (π r₁) (π r₂)).op (S r₂)
      simp only [Functor.comp_map, Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op] at n1 n2
      rw [hS'def, hS'def, ← n1, ← n2]
      exact hcc' (r₁, r₂)
    rw [← hq1, ← hq2, op_comp, op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply,
      Functor.map_comp_apply, inner]
  obtain ⟨T, hT, -⟩ :=
    (Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff (P := (F m').obj) (π := fun r => (D.u c₀).map (π r))).1
      (isSheafFor_of_mem_toPrecoverage D F m' hcovm') S' hcompat
  -- the glued section at level `m'` is the one we were given
  have hZ' : (u m').obj ((D.u c₀).obj ((D.u a₀).obj Y₀)) = Z :=
    ((Functor.congr_obj (hu c₀) ((D.u a₀).obj Y₀)).trans (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) Y₀)).trans hZ
  have hR' : Presieve.ofArrows (fun r => (u i₀).obj (B r)) mr ∈ K Z := by
    rw [hK]
    refine ⟨i₀, Y₀, hZ, Presieve.ofArrows B g, hcov, hfin, ?_⟩
    subst hZ
    rw [Presieve.map_ofArrows]
    congr 1
    funext r
    rw [hmrdef]
    simp
  refine ⟨m', (D.u c₀).obj ((D.u a₀).obj Y₀), hZ', T, ?_⟩
  refine eq_of_map_eq_of_mem K G _ hR' _ t ?_
  rintro W f ⟨r⟩
  have cclaim :
    (u m').map ((D.u c₀).map (π r)) =
      eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu c₀) ((D.u a₀).obj (B r))) ≫
        eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r)) ≫ mr r ≫ eqToHom hZ'.symm := by
    have h1 : (u m').map ((D.u c₀).map (π r)) = (D.u c₀ ⋙ u m').map (π r) := rfl
    have h2 : (u m).map (π r) = (D.u a₀ ⋙ u m).map (g r) := by
      rw [hπ]; rfl
    rw [h1, Functor.congr_hom (hu c₀) (π r), h2, Functor.congr_hom (hu a₀) (g r), hmrdef]
    simp
  have key2 :
    eqToHom (congrArg op hZ') ≫ (mr r).op =
      ((u m').map ((D.u c₀).map (π r))).op ≫
        eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu c₀) ((D.u a₀).obj (B r)))) ≫
        eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a₀) (B r))) := by
    rw [cclaim]
    simp
  rw [ht (mr r) (hmr r), ← hSι r, hι c₀ ((D.u a₀).obj (B r)) (S r), ← hS'def r, ← hT r,
    NatTrans.naturality_apply (ι m') ((D.u c₀).map (π r)).op T]
  simp only [Functor.comp_map, Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op]
  simp only [← Functor.map_comp_apply]
  rw [key2]
  simp

include hu hobj hhom hhom_inj hK hψ hι hG in
/-- **Every section of `G` comes from a level**: the induction on the closure of the image family
under restriction and gluing, whose base and restriction steps are `comesFromLevel_of_map` and
whose gluing step is `comesFromLevel_amalgamate`. -/
private lemma comesFromLevel_all (V : C) (s : G.obj.obj (op V)) : ComesFromLevel ι V s := by
  have h := subsheafClosure_imageSubfunctor D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ G ι hι hG V s
  induction h with
  | @base Z a hmem =>
    obtain ⟨k, Y, p, x, rfl⟩ := hmem
    exact comesFromLevel_of_map D u hu hobj hhom K F ψ G ι hι Z k Y p x
  | @restrict Z W f a _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨k, Y, e, t, ht⟩ := ih
    have h1 : G.obj.map (f ≫ eqToHom e.symm).op ((ι k).app (op Y) t) = G.obj.map f.op a := by
      rw [← ht, op_comp, eqToHom_op, Functor.map_comp_apply]
    rw [← h1]
    exact comesFromLevel_of_map D u hu hobj hhom K F ψ G ι hι Z k Y (f ≫ eqToHom e.symm) t
  | @amalgamate Z R hR y hy _ t ht ih =>
    exact
      comesFromLevel_amalgamate D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ G ι hι hG Z R hR y hy ih t ht

end

end

end Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections

@[expose] public section

open Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSheafSections in
/-- **Sections of a colimit of sheaves on a colimit of sites.** In the situation of Stacks 0A34,
let the functors `u i : D.C i ⥤ C` exhibit the small category `C` as the colimit of the `D.C i`
(`hu`, `hobj`, `hhom`, `hhom_inj`) and let `K` be the collection of coverings of `C` of
Stacks 09YL (`hK`), so that each `u i` defines a morphism of sites `f_i : C → C_i`
(Stacks 0A35).

Let `F i` be a sheaf of sets on `(D.C i, D.J i)` for every `i`, and for `a : j ⟶ i` let
`ψ a : F i ⟶ f_{a,*}F j` be the adjoint of a map `φ_a : f_a^{-1}F_i → F_j` of sheaves on `D.C j`,
subject to the cocycle condition `hψ`. Let `G` be the colimit `colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i`, presented by
its universal property: `ι i` is the adjoint of the structure map `f_i^{-1}F_i ⟶ G` (`hι`) and
every compatible family of maps to a sheaf `H` on `C` factors uniquely through it (`hG`).

Then for every object `X` of `D.C i` the sections of `G` over `u_i(X)` are the filtered colimit
over the arrows `a : j ⟶ i` of the sections of `F j` over `u_a(X)`: the canonical maps `ρ a`
(`hρ`) are jointly surjective, and two sections of `F j` over `u_a(X)` with the same image under
`ρ a` agree after applying `ψ b` for some `b : k ⟶ j`. -/
@[stacks 09YN "weak-system variant (Stacks 00VH finite coverings): The sections over `u_i(X_i)` of \
  the colimit `colim f_i^{-1}F_i` of a system of
  sheaves on an inverse system of sites are the filtered colimit of the sections `F_j(u_a(X_i))`
  over the arrows `a : j → i`."]
public theorem InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.sections_colimit_pullback_of_colimit {C : Type w}
    [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaves `F i` and, in adjoint form, the maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}F_i → F_j`
    (F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj)
    -- the cocycle condition `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a`
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j k : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (b : k ⟶ j) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
        (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) x =
          (F k).obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp b a) V).symm))
            ((ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    -- `G = colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i`, presented by its universal property
    (G : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)) (ι : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ G.obj)
    (hι :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
        (ι i).app (op V) x =
          G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
            ((ι j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    (hG :
      ∀ (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)) (g : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj),
        (∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
            (g i).app (op V) x =
              H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
                ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x))) →
          ∃! h : G ⟶ H,
            ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
              (g i).app (op V) x = h.hom.app (op ((u i).obj V)) ((ι i).app (op V) x))
    (i : D.I) (X : D.C i)
    -- the canonical maps `F_j(u_a(X)) → G(u_i(X))`
    (ρ :
      ∀ {j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F j).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X)) → G.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj X)))
    (hρ :
      ∀ {j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (t : (F j).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X))),
        ρ a t =
          G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X)))
            ((ι j).app (op ((D.u a).obj X)) t)) :
    -- every section of `G` over `u_i(X)` comes from some level below `i`
    (∀ s : G.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj X)),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (t : (F j).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X))), ρ a t = s) ∧
      -- two sections with the same image agree at a further level
      ∀ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (t t' : (F j).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X))),
        ρ a t = ρ a t' →
          ∃ (k : D.I) (b : k ⟶ j),
            (ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj X)) t = (ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj X)) t' := by
  refine ⟨fun s => ?_, fun j a t t' hyp => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨k, Y, e, w, rfl⟩ :=
      comesFromLevel_all D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ G ι hι hG ((u i).obj X) s
    obtain ⟨m, b, t, hb⟩ := exists_level_of_hom D u hu hhom K F ψ G ι hι i X k Y (eqToHom e.symm) w
    refine ⟨m, b, t, ?_⟩
    rw [hρ b t, hb, eqToHom_op]
  · refine
      exists_ψ_eq_of_ι_eq D u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ G ι hG j ((D.u a).obj X) t t' ?_
    refine map_eqToHom_injective G.obj (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X)) ?_
    rw [← hρ a t, ← hρ a t']
    exact hyp

end

end

end CategoryTheory.Sites.InverseSystem
